WEBVTT

00:15.780 --> 00:18.070
There are as many people
as there are stars...

00:18.620 --> 00:20.950
There are as many encounters
as there are stars...

00:21.410 --> 00:23.290
And farewells...

00:31.210 --> 00:33.100
I'll be going now.

00:33.090 --> 00:35.270
Misumaru Family Grave

00:33.800 --> 00:34.720
Yurika...

00:35.970 --> 00:40.190
Are you getting along well with Akito, Yurika?

00:41.730 --> 00:46.150
Terminal Colony Number 8 - Shirahime

00:42.140 --> 00:44.230
Yamabuki Platoon, give backup to Blue!

00:44.730 --> 00:46.150
Roger!

00:51.650 --> 00:53.790
Orange and Vermilion stay at
your current position.

00:52.530 --> 00:54.620
First and Second platoon, decimated!

00:53.780 --> 00:55.500
Red, pull back to point Alpha!

00:54.820 --> 00:55.500
Damn it!

01:01.830 --> 01:02.810
Wait!

01:02.810 --> 01:05.090
If you kill us, then the research...

01:05.960 --> 01:07.050
Secrecy demands your silence.

01:08.500 --> 01:09.980
Purple Eye, fall back!

01:09.980 --> 01:11.010
Purple Eye!

01:13.550 --> 01:16.770
The belated man of revenge... So callow.

01:17.340 --> 01:18.130
Vanish!

01:25.140 --> 01:28.110
United Earth Space Fleet Third Fleet Battleship Amaryllis

01:26.730 --> 01:28.110
Shirahime? Shirahime?

01:28.650 --> 01:29.910
Please respond!

01:29.440 --> 01:31.200
Highest priority on retrieval of all injured!

01:29.900 --> 01:31.530
Shirahime! Shirahime!

01:31.190 --> 01:32.830
Raise field and approach!

01:31.520 --> 01:32.820
Please respond!

01:33.780 --> 01:35.030
Bose particles increasing!

01:35.030 --> 01:35.660
What?

01:36.690 --> 01:37.580
Magnifying image on screen!

01:40.490 --> 01:41.810
Change sensors!

01:41.810 --> 01:42.340
Aye!

01:44.620 --> 01:46.760
What... What is that...?

01:48.670 --> 01:50.180
What is this?

01:51.330 --> 01:58.890
MARTIAN SUCCESSOR NADESICO

02:03.150 --> 02:05.680
The United Earth has called for the
emergency General Assembly to be...

02:05.680 --> 02:07.610
...convened in an effort to decide
upon measures in response to...

02:10.730 --> 02:11.790
Did you hear?

02:11.790 --> 02:12.320
What?

02:12.590 --> 02:14.240
It actually appeared, they said!

02:14.570 --> 02:16.450
Of course, it's only a rumor.

02:16.450 --> 02:19.280
It came out of nowhere and said,
"I curse you all."

02:21.280 --> 02:22.670
Ghost...

02:22.670 --> 02:24.130
...Robot?

02:31.750 --> 02:33.550
The Hisago Plan!

02:34.000 --> 02:36.710
The grand web that spans space,
the Hisago Plan...

02:37.050 --> 02:39.260
Four of the colonies that
make up part of this network...

02:39.260 --> 02:40.760
...have been destroyed one after another!

02:40.760 --> 02:42.020
Four in a row!

02:42.020 --> 02:44.240
For what purpose? Who is doing this?

02:44.240 --> 02:45.860
This cannot be forgiven!

02:46.240 --> 02:49.490
We're not going to go with
"Saturn Lizards" this time, are we?

02:49.770 --> 02:52.170
What? What is that supposed to mean?!

02:52.170 --> 02:55.520
One source has attributed all this to
a conspiracy by a certain nation.

02:56.070 --> 02:57.610
Shut up, lizard breath!

02:57.610 --> 02:58.820
We heard the same thing about you as well!

02:58.820 --> 03:00.820
What was that?! Outside! Now!

03:02.660 --> 03:05.370
Order! Please everyone, order!

03:06.580 --> 03:09.460
This has been footage from the floor
of the United Earth General Assembly.

03:09.950 --> 03:11.120
I saw it!

03:11.790 --> 03:13.430
It was a boson jump!

03:14.130 --> 03:17.130
But didn't reports indicate that
the explosion of the colony...

03:17.130 --> 03:19.880
...was wreaking havoc on
the sensors of nearby ships?

03:20.220 --> 03:21.950
Are you saying my observation was mistaken?

03:21.950 --> 03:23.190
Exactly!

03:23.190 --> 03:24.400
Think about it!

03:24.930 --> 03:28.810
Neither the Earth nor the
Jovian Federation is capable...

03:28.810 --> 03:31.860
...of building an eight-meter
tall robot that can boson jump!

03:32.070 --> 03:32.820
Damn it!

03:32.820 --> 03:34.770
Come, come, no need for that.

03:35.190 --> 03:37.680
Those numbskulls aren't at all serious
about getting to the bottom of this.

03:37.680 --> 03:39.320
Some Accident Investigations Committee!

03:39.320 --> 03:41.990
And so the United Earth Space Fleet
is left out in the cold.

03:41.990 --> 03:44.280
This is to be a joint investigation
in the hands of the...

03:44.280 --> 03:46.160
...Investigations Committee and
the Unified Forces Command.

03:46.160 --> 03:47.160
Admiral!

03:48.330 --> 03:51.630
Well, I suppose we can't just sit
and watch everything happen.

03:51.630 --> 03:53.510
That's why I've already dispatched yours truly...

03:53.750 --> 03:55.170
The Nadesico.

03:56.080 --> 03:57.090
The Nadesico?

04:10.350 --> 04:11.730
Hello...

04:14.980 --> 04:16.660
Sabu-chan!

04:16.660 --> 04:18.830
I haven't heard from you for quite a while.

04:18.830 --> 04:20.110
You owe us!

04:20.900 --> 04:22.120
Hey, Sabu!

04:22.650 --> 04:24.280
Why haven't you called me back?

04:24.280 --> 04:26.280
You'd better not be playing
around with other women,

04:26.280 --> 04:28.370
or else I'm going to make you pay!

04:29.700 --> 04:31.880
This has been your visual
answering machine service.

04:30.620 --> 04:33.000
The girls are all over you,
aren't they, Mr. Saburota?

04:33.000 --> 04:34.250
Oh, you were watching?

04:34.620 --> 04:36.580
How could I miss it?

04:36.580 --> 04:37.510
Oh, yeah.

04:38.000 --> 04:40.500
I was under the impression that officers...

04:40.500 --> 04:43.380
...of the Jovian Federation were all
very dedicated and gallant.

04:43.880 --> 04:47.090
Well, I appreciate you thinking that.

04:47.550 --> 04:48.760
Lieutenant Takasugi!

04:49.300 --> 04:52.070
Confirming the terminal colony
Takiri dead ahead.

05:09.130 --> 05:11.630
Increasing distortion field to maximum power!

05:11.630 --> 05:12.730
Confirming route.

05:12.730 --> 05:15.590
Takiri to Sayori to Tagitsu to
final destination, Amaterasu!

05:21.790 --> 05:23.670
Raise optical barrier.

05:24.050 --> 05:25.980
All hands, please go through
final check procedure.

05:26.230 --> 05:27.630
Closing communications links.

05:27.630 --> 05:29.400
Living quarters readied for jump.

05:29.400 --> 05:30.930
Energy systems, are okay to go!

05:31.350 --> 05:33.480
Ship alert status pattern B!

05:33.480 --> 05:34.890
No abnormality in field output.

05:34.890 --> 05:36.650
And everything else checks out a-okay!

05:36.640 --> 05:37.950
GOOD JOB!

05:41.440 --> 05:43.520
Fermion to boson conversion
proceeding normally.

05:43.900 --> 05:45.110
All decks condition Green.

05:45.440 --> 05:49.870
Increasing intensity level... 6, 7, 8, 9...

05:50.820 --> 05:51.500
Jump.

05:57.460 --> 06:00.720
Ladies and gentlemen, welcome to
the terminal colony, Amaterasu.

06:01.250 --> 06:04.840
From the United Earth Space Fleet Fourth Fleet,

06:05.210 --> 06:07.240
this is the experimental battleship Nadesico B.

06:07.240 --> 06:09.300
We request navigational assistance to Amaterasu.

06:09.300 --> 06:10.010
Acknowledged.

06:10.010 --> 06:12.360
And it's all work from here.

06:11.760 --> 06:13.230
Mr. Saburota!

06:18.890 --> 06:21.460
Navigation system, connect to Amaterasu.

06:21.460 --> 06:23.480
Requesting guidance for parking and docking.

06:23.480 --> 06:24.320
Acknowledged.

06:28.610 --> 06:30.430
Who the hell are you?!

06:30.430 --> 06:34.060
Lieutenant Commander Ruri Hoshino,
United Earth Space Fleet.

06:34.060 --> 06:37.210
Lieutenant Saburota Takasugi, UESF as well.

06:37.550 --> 06:39.580
I don't care about any of that!

06:40.290 --> 06:42.000
What I want to know is what
the hell are you doing here?!

06:42.000 --> 06:44.630
I am not aware of any issues
that would arise from...

06:44.630 --> 06:47.380
...UESF entering into UE property
such as this colony.

06:47.960 --> 06:50.240
This is the central core of the Hisago Plan!

06:50.240 --> 06:51.810
Did you get permission from
the Development Corporation?!

06:52.180 --> 06:53.780
We wouldn't be here if we didn't get it.

06:53.780 --> 06:54.930
What was that?!

06:54.930 --> 06:57.830
Oh, no, that was just his
Yokohama dialect kicking in.

06:57.830 --> 06:58.280
No really.

06:58.640 --> 07:00.980
In the previous Shirahime Incident,

07:00.980 --> 07:03.650
an abnormal increase of bosons were reported.

07:04.020 --> 07:06.940
If there are any problems with the
management of the jump system,

07:06.940 --> 07:10.250
the adjacent navigation routes
and colonies will be affected.

07:10.900 --> 07:13.610
The emergency inspection clause of
the Colony Administration Law...

07:13.610 --> 07:15.990
...can be applied to such cases,
so please understand.

07:15.990 --> 07:18.710
Hell, just think of this as
being a gas leak inspection.

07:19.160 --> 07:21.240
There are no shortcomings in the Hisago Plan!

07:21.240 --> 07:22.680
Please, Admiral.

07:23.000 --> 07:24.830
"To protect the peace of greater space,"

07:24.830 --> 07:27.130
is the stated mission of our dear UE Space Fleet.

07:27.550 --> 07:29.630
Let us have faith in the
Commander who is passionate...

07:29.630 --> 07:31.560
...about fulfilling her duty as part of that mission.

07:33.640 --> 07:35.810
Hello, everyone!

07:35.810 --> 07:37.820
Hello!

07:37.820 --> 07:40.520
Welcome to the guided tour
of the Hisago Plan,

07:40.520 --> 07:43.440
the research center for the transportation
mode of the future, boson jumping!

07:43.440 --> 07:45.690
Your guide will be me, Mayumi, and...

07:45.690 --> 07:46.740
Me, Hisagon!

07:47.020 --> 07:49.190
And today we have a special guest among us.

07:49.530 --> 07:52.450
Today, your tour around this facility
will be accompanied by the...

07:52.450 --> 07:53.210
Yes, the...

07:53.210 --> 07:56.410
The youngest ever captain and
the beautiful child prodigy,

07:56.410 --> 07:59.510
Lieutenant Commander Ruri Hoshino
of the United Earth Space Fleet.

07:59.510 --> 08:00.410
Nice to meet you.

08:03.580 --> 08:05.920
An inspection with children accompanying?

08:05.920 --> 08:07.250
Oh, I just love this!

08:09.630 --> 08:13.060
I feel sorry for the Commander with
what we're making her go through.

08:13.590 --> 08:16.150
I suppose the Space Fleet
Command feels they need...

08:16.150 --> 08:17.610
...to save face regarding these latest incidents.

08:17.610 --> 08:19.960
Space Fleet Command has no face to save!

08:19.960 --> 08:21.700
What is that brat doing here?!

08:21.700 --> 08:24.240
It's just them making a point,
the Space Fleet of course.

08:24.240 --> 08:26.270
We can think of her as a
simple child on an errand.

08:28.690 --> 08:29.120
Then better to send the
kid back as soon as we can!

08:36.280 --> 08:37.420
Well...

08:37.700 --> 08:40.700
All sectors clear up to 11001.

08:41.040 --> 08:42.500
Ready to go?

08:43.580 --> 08:45.170
Search data, silk-strained.

08:46.080 --> 08:48.130
Relay the soups to me once they're done.

08:48.500 --> 08:50.600
Hold speed steady at moderate wanko rate.

08:50.990 --> 08:51.470
Yo!

08:54.840 --> 08:56.590
Why did you get so spooked like that?

08:57.470 --> 08:59.180
Please don't enter the window bowl...

08:59.180 --> 09:01.140
...without asking me first.

09:01.560 --> 09:02.600
Oh, come on.

09:02.600 --> 09:04.770
It's not as if we're strangers that
never spent lots of time together.

09:04.770 --> 09:07.980
W... What?! What are you saying,
you sex crazed maniac?!

09:10.820 --> 09:12.600
But is this right?

09:12.600 --> 09:15.250
What now? You're really prone
to mood swings, aren't you?

09:15.250 --> 09:17.450
But this is hacking.

09:17.780 --> 09:20.070
Even if they are not willing to cooperate...

09:20.070 --> 09:21.590
What else can we do?

09:21.590 --> 09:23.330
It looks like both the
Investigations Committee and...

09:23.330 --> 09:25.000
...the Unified Forces are hiding something.

09:25.330 --> 09:29.460
But... this is so unfair to the Captain.

09:31.130 --> 09:35.380
Is this the mouth that's getting
so sentimental all of a sudden?

09:36.510 --> 09:39.850
Hey, the Captain is nice enough to
play the part of being the clown.

09:40.510 --> 09:43.100
Let's use this opportunity to get
as much as we can, all right?

09:43.600 --> 09:44.570
Okay...

09:44.930 --> 09:49.170
And that's it on the difficult subject
of super-symmetry and such!

09:49.170 --> 09:50.460
Did you all understand it?

09:50.460 --> 09:52.530
I don't get it!

09:52.830 --> 09:56.280
Well in other words,
by going through these Chulips,

09:56.280 --> 09:58.820
it's possible to travel between long distances,

09:58.820 --> 10:01.790
such as from Earth to Mars.

10:05.160 --> 10:10.020
But at this point, normal people
are not able to use this system.

10:10.020 --> 10:14.890
If regular people need to use this,
they need to have their bodies...

10:15.110 --> 10:16.550
Re-engineered?

10:17.550 --> 10:20.870
Well, it's not like they have to do that much.

10:20.870 --> 10:23.400
They take the DNA and...

10:21.180 --> 10:23.390
Hey, I heard about it on the TV.

10:23.390 --> 10:25.340
They, well, adjust it so that...

10:23.390 --> 10:25.340
Something about it being inhumane and stuff.

10:25.340 --> 10:26.390
Oh, really?

10:26.390 --> 10:28.850
You don't have to be
oversensitive on my account.

10:28.850 --> 10:29.820
Oh, well yes...

10:30.350 --> 10:34.570
Right now, for a regular person to
be able to boson jump on their own,

10:34.570 --> 10:37.110
they have to have their DNA altered a little.

10:38.290 --> 10:40.510
Are you a re-engineered person, Commander?

10:40.510 --> 10:41.160
Yes, I am.

10:42.030 --> 10:43.560
Wow! It's true!

10:43.560 --> 10:46.950
But actually, if you use a
powerful enough distortion field,

10:46.950 --> 10:49.960
then a normal person can go
through a boson jump too.

10:49.960 --> 10:51.220
Like on board a military vessel.

10:54.250 --> 10:56.140
Welcome to Amaterasu!

10:58.090 --> 10:59.600
Yup, here we go.

11:00.050 --> 11:02.680
There are entire blocks that aren't
listed in the official blue prints.

11:03.140 --> 11:05.350
I guess there are reasons why
all these raids are taking place.

11:05.720 --> 11:07.270
Come on, let's dive in!

11:10.600 --> 11:12.730
Human experiments in boson jumping?

11:13.770 --> 11:15.720
This is all unsanctioned.

11:15.720 --> 11:17.150
Hey, these guys are all...

11:17.900 --> 11:22.500
WARNING

11:18.730 --> 11:19.650
Did we blow it?

11:20.070 --> 11:21.250
Release mode!

11:21.250 --> 11:22.500
Omoikane, data block, now!

11:23.610 --> 11:25.460
Guide intruding program to bypass!

11:25.830 --> 11:26.420
What?!

11:27.620 --> 11:28.950
What the hell is this?

11:31.710 --> 11:32.580
Welcome...

11:33.420 --> 11:35.180
Welcome to Amaterasu.

11:35.750 --> 11:37.640
Welcome to Amaterasu.

11:37.920 --> 11:39.600
Welcome to Amaterasu.

11:40.840 --> 11:42.270
What the hell is this?

11:42.270 --> 11:44.550
Get this under control now! Pronto!

11:44.890 --> 11:47.230
Yes! Imagine if we fall under attack now!

11:47.230 --> 11:49.820
Cut line thirteen and give priority to line fifteen!

11:47.760 --> 11:48.930
Yes, yes!

11:48.930 --> 11:51.610
We're doing the best we can
to get things under control.

11:49.810 --> 11:51.630
Halt all window communications!

11:51.630 --> 11:52.730
This is Operations.

11:52.730 --> 11:55.700
Please calm down. Yes, this
will all be under control soon.

11:54.020 --> 11:55.700
Oh, nothing, Sir.

11:56.360 --> 11:59.530
Contact with windows will not cause any harm.

12:00.160 --> 12:01.870
Please remain calm.

12:04.410 --> 12:07.070
Please calm down. Everyone please!

12:07.530 --> 12:10.630
Form two lines now. Come on, keep quiet.

12:07.910 --> 12:09.660
Did you screw up, Hari?

12:09.660 --> 12:11.260
It wasn't me!

12:10.620 --> 12:13.340
I said shut up! Hey! Pipe down!

12:11.250 --> 12:13.670
Amaterasu's computers are
fighting amongst themselves!

12:13.330 --> 12:15.510
All right, let's all get in line now.

12:13.660 --> 12:14.380
Fighting?

12:14.380 --> 12:16.840
Yes, that's right! Exactly!

12:16.840 --> 12:20.230
Amaterasu contains an
unofficial system within itself.

12:20.230 --> 12:23.510
It seems the unknown system is
revealing its presence to everyone...

12:23.510 --> 12:27.310
...or just laughing out loud,
and that's making all this mess.

12:28.520 --> 12:30.270
Windows are safe.

12:28.520 --> 12:29.470
What? Captain?!

12:29.470 --> 12:31.820
Where are you going, Captain?

12:30.260 --> 12:32.860
Everyone, please remain calm.

12:31.810 --> 12:34.240
Oh, please wait for me, Captain!

12:32.850 --> 12:34.240
I repeat...

12:36.200 --> 12:39.800
Captain, could you please hold on
just a second! Where are you going?

12:39.800 --> 12:41.330
I'm heading back to the Nadesico.

12:41.330 --> 12:42.050
What?

12:42.050 --> 12:43.150
The enemy will come soon!

12:43.150 --> 12:43.650
What?!

12:46.990 --> 12:48.580
Increased reading of Bose particles!

12:53.580 --> 12:55.230
Total height, approximately ten meters.

12:55.230 --> 12:56.540
Width, approximately fifteen meters!

12:56.540 --> 12:58.800
Target cannot be identified.
Not responding to any hails.

13:02.760 --> 13:04.850
Sorry! Excuse us!

13:06.980 --> 13:08.970
I can't say how much I appreciate this.

13:08.970 --> 13:10.100
Oh, don't worry.

13:10.550 --> 13:12.430
Doesn't this get you all excited and stuff?

13:13.930 --> 13:16.340
My premonition was right.
The enemy came.

13:16.340 --> 13:17.950
Was that a code? Or a coincidence?

13:18.730 --> 13:19.950
But he...

13:20.200 --> 13:21.320
But they both...

13:23.230 --> 13:24.290
Ruri-chan!

13:26.320 --> 13:26.870
INTERCEPT

13:39.640 --> 13:41.420
Keep it away from the colony!

13:39.640 --> 13:41.420
3rd Company, move back.

13:41.420 --> 13:42.850
Lay down covering fire!

13:41.420 --> 13:42.850
Kirutansasu, hold your current position!

13:42.850 --> 13:45.140
No pain, no gain!

13:45.490 --> 13:47.930
W-What are you talking about, Admiral?

13:48.510 --> 13:52.070
I'm permitting the use of weapons
near and inside the colony!

13:52.070 --> 13:52.800
What?!

13:52.800 --> 13:55.220
B-But Admiral, the colony will be...

13:55.600 --> 13:58.110
Easier to strike at a fly that has
attached itself to something.

13:59.020 --> 14:01.240
I will allow some sacrifices to be made!

14:01.240 --> 14:02.570
I gotcha!

14:06.030 --> 14:07.370
Time to move out, you bums!

14:07.370 --> 14:08.070
Aye!

14:16.260 --> 14:16.550
EVASIVE
ACTION

14:17.760 --> 14:18.510
Too slow!

14:22.630 --> 14:24.100
All right? Can you move?

14:24.100 --> 14:24.970
Damn...

14:25.920 --> 14:26.310
Sorry!

14:30.300 --> 14:31.400
Sorry for the delay.

14:31.730 --> 14:32.770
WELCOME HOME

14:33.050 --> 14:36.100
Go into combat mode and standby.

14:36.560 --> 14:38.480
We will monitor the situation for awhile.

14:38.480 --> 14:40.240
We're not going to join in?

14:40.240 --> 14:41.770
Nadesico B's priority will be the...

14:41.770 --> 14:43.790
...orderly evacuation of personnel from the colony.

14:43.790 --> 14:47.370
Besides, it appears that they don't want our help.

14:47.370 --> 14:48.200
I see...

14:48.200 --> 14:49.200
That's right!

14:49.490 --> 14:52.200
The Unified Forces has now become
an invincible military force...

14:52.200 --> 14:55.200
...ready to defeat the enemy on
land, sea, air, or in space!

14:55.200 --> 14:57.670
The Space Fleet is but an obsolete relic!

14:57.670 --> 15:00.210
Just sit back and enjoy the view!

15:02.670 --> 15:04.380
He sure is pumped up.

15:04.710 --> 15:07.840
Hari, hack into Amaterasu once more.

15:07.840 --> 15:09.300
What? Again?

15:09.630 --> 15:10.140
Yes...

15:10.590 --> 15:13.170
The keyword is "Akito."

15:13.170 --> 15:13.800
What?

15:13.800 --> 15:16.110
Akito? What is that?

15:16.110 --> 15:18.070
Hey, Captain? Captain?!

15:18.430 --> 15:21.670
Raise IFS feedback to level 10.

15:21.670 --> 15:24.030
All stations, go to alert status pattern A.

15:24.980 --> 15:26.450
Start total systems control.

15:29.070 --> 15:30.040
Akito...

15:30.320 --> 15:32.500
Stop saying "Akito, Akito" all the time!

15:37.960 --> 15:39.660
Damn it, stop getting in my way!

15:39.660 --> 15:40.840
That's my target!

15:41.620 --> 15:43.850
The enemy has moved back
to the second defense line.

15:43.850 --> 15:46.300
Friendly high mobile units
are continuing with pursuit.

15:47.640 --> 15:49.780
There you see, Shinjyuu.

15:49.780 --> 15:53.470
This is the might of the Unified Forces.
The new force!

15:53.470 --> 15:54.090
I see...

15:54.090 --> 15:55.720
Damn Space Fleet deadbeats.

15:55.720 --> 15:59.360
They may have pushed people around
during the war, but not anymore!

15:59.360 --> 16:02.390
Banzai for the United Earth
Unified Peace Keeping Forces!

16:02.390 --> 16:04.070
Banzai for the Hisago Plan!

16:04.470 --> 16:06.170
Increased reading of Bose particles!

16:06.170 --> 16:06.570
What?

16:11.330 --> 16:13.550
The guard units have taken a
gravity blast on their flank.

16:13.550 --> 16:14.670
Heavy losses!

16:14.670 --> 16:15.910
Estimating total mass...

16:15.910 --> 16:17.240
It's a battleship class unit!

16:20.080 --> 16:22.150
A battleship that can jump?

16:22.150 --> 16:23.690
Do you think it's Nergal?

16:23.690 --> 16:24.670
Hard to say...

16:25.040 --> 16:26.290
What about them?

16:26.290 --> 16:27.920
They said, "be here in five minutes."

16:27.920 --> 16:29.260
Oh boy, this is close!

16:30.000 --> 16:32.340
Emergency orders!
Evacuation in five minutes!

16:33.220 --> 16:35.300
Hello to all evacuees on board.

16:35.930 --> 16:38.110
I'm the captain of this ship,
Lieutenant Commander Hoshino.

16:38.420 --> 16:40.850
The Nadesico will leave
Amaterasu and move out to...

16:40.850 --> 16:44.070
...the second defense line to aid
in the rescue of the injured.

16:46.030 --> 16:48.660
Nadesico B has left its port in Amaterasu!

16:48.660 --> 16:50.490
Who cares about a brat like her!

16:50.490 --> 16:52.450
Counterattack against the enemy battleship!

16:52.830 --> 16:55.070
Bring the Kirutantasu and Yoimachizuki about.

16:55.070 --> 16:55.990
Now!

16:55.990 --> 16:56.420
Yes, Sir!

17:02.330 --> 17:04.620
Lapis, Lapis...

17:05.580 --> 17:06.460
Lapis...

17:07.330 --> 17:08.300
Lapis!

17:14.340 --> 17:15.270
Damn it!

17:15.850 --> 17:16.890
I'm after him!

17:17.600 --> 17:19.230
Get the hell out of my way!

17:26.100 --> 17:27.150
There!

17:31.580 --> 17:33.120
You suck!

17:33.120 --> 17:34.370
We'll cover you.

17:34.370 --> 17:35.540
If you can keep up!

17:39.670 --> 17:42.340
The sudden attack and raid.

17:42.340 --> 17:45.880
A diversion from an ambush
masked as a counterattack.

17:45.880 --> 17:49.510
All the while another raid,
now from a different attack route.

17:50.290 --> 17:51.600
That's something.

17:51.600 --> 17:53.880
Ms. Ryoko is amazing as
well for catching on to this.

17:54.250 --> 17:55.260
What do we do?

17:55.920 --> 17:57.440
Let's wait a little more.

17:57.440 --> 17:58.310
What?

17:58.310 --> 17:59.520
The enemy's objective...

18:00.180 --> 18:02.070
The enemy's true objective...

18:02.070 --> 18:03.440
Aren't you interested in finding out?

18:08.270 --> 18:08.980
Jettison!

18:09.780 --> 18:10.910
Jettisoning!

18:10.910 --> 18:12.200
What?!

18:19.040 --> 18:20.180
Damn it!

18:20.180 --> 18:22.600
You think you're Gekigangar?!

18:22.600 --> 18:24.060
Shoot it down!

18:24.060 --> 18:26.670
Fire, fire, and fire some more!

18:27.540 --> 18:29.260
Fire!

18:30.800 --> 18:32.590
Fire everything you got!

18:37.170 --> 18:38.770
Bastard!

18:40.510 --> 18:41.520
Fire!

18:41.520 --> 18:42.620
Shoot it down!

18:42.620 --> 18:44.350
Shoot to kill!

18:44.810 --> 18:46.190
You jackasses!

18:46.410 --> 18:48.050
You're just getting in the way!

18:48.050 --> 18:49.350
Shut up and get out!

18:49.810 --> 18:50.870
What was that?!

18:50.870 --> 18:52.390
I haven't got time for you!

18:52.390 --> 18:54.200
You're in my way!

18:54.200 --> 18:55.850
You're the one who's in the way!

18:55.850 --> 18:57.650
Why you...!

18:58.940 --> 19:01.460
The gate is open. Is that a good idea?

19:02.030 --> 19:02.870
What?

19:05.870 --> 19:07.640
Gate Number 13, opening.

19:07.120 --> 19:08.960
Gate 13

19:07.120 --> 19:08.960
"Ruin" Docking Bay

19:07.120 --> 19:08.960
GATE OPEN

19:07.640 --> 19:08.960
It's the enemy's hacking!

19:09.370 --> 19:11.520
Thirteen? What is that?

19:11.520 --> 19:12.670
I don't know anything about this.

19:12.670 --> 19:14.920
As it so happens, there is a Gate 13, Admiral.

19:15.420 --> 19:16.780
What is that supposed to mean?

19:16.780 --> 19:19.430
It means that the charade is over.

19:20.670 --> 19:22.390
That man's persistence...

19:27.690 --> 19:28.680
Eat this!

19:33.940 --> 19:36.280
It has been quite some time, Ms. Ryoko.

19:36.280 --> 19:38.310
Yeah, about two years now.

19:38.310 --> 19:39.440
You're looking good.

19:39.820 --> 19:41.780
You certainly are amazing, as always.

19:42.700 --> 19:45.490
Hell, knocking over unmanned
drones doesn't amount to anything.

19:45.490 --> 19:47.580
It would seem that they are
part of a trap designed to...

19:47.580 --> 19:49.540
...counter any intruder,
regardless of friend or foe.

19:49.540 --> 19:50.710
Oh?

19:51.250 --> 19:53.440
There are no more traps ahead.

19:53.440 --> 19:54.620
I'll guide you from here.

19:54.620 --> 19:55.710
Thanks...

19:56.180 --> 19:59.850
Hey, you've hacked into somebody
else's system, haven't you?!

19:59.850 --> 20:02.090
The enemy is doing it as well,
and this is an emergency.

20:02.090 --> 20:05.720
Oh, the person actually doing
the work is Hari, right here.

20:06.140 --> 20:07.720
Captain, how mean!

20:16.270 --> 20:18.490
The enemy has reached the fifth isolation firewall.

20:18.790 --> 20:20.450
Initiate Plan B!

20:20.450 --> 20:23.040
Dispatch to all branches, "Carry out calmly."

20:20.900 --> 20:22.030
Let me go!

20:22.030 --> 20:23.580
I'm not going to run!

20:23.040 --> 20:23.570
Yes, Sir!

20:23.570 --> 20:25.130
Admiral, please be quiet.

20:25.130 --> 20:26.420
Lieutenant Colonel Shinjyuu...

20:27.070 --> 20:28.330
What are you doing?!

20:28.660 --> 20:30.370
Who the hell are you?!

20:31.250 --> 20:35.870
Enemy of Earth... Enemy of Jupiter...
Enemy of all corruption...

20:35.870 --> 20:36.640
What?!

20:37.330 --> 20:38.340
We are...

20:38.890 --> 20:40.600
The Martian Successors!

20:53.180 --> 20:55.560
All right, keep it right there.

20:59.400 --> 21:01.190
I was just asked to do this.

21:01.530 --> 21:03.290
This girl here wants to talk to you.

21:04.240 --> 21:08.920
Hello, I'm Lieutenant Commander Ruri
Hoshino of the UE Space Fleet.

21:09.620 --> 21:11.200
I'm sorry for being so pushy,

21:11.200 --> 21:15.080
but since you locked out
all window communication links,

21:15.080 --> 21:17.170
I asked Ms. Ryoko to act as a relay.

21:19.330 --> 21:21.390
Please tell me...

21:21.800 --> 21:23.810
Who might you be?

21:24.510 --> 21:25.700
Who are you?

21:25.700 --> 21:27.840
Lapis, analyze password.

21:36.390 --> 21:38.060
Please enter the password, okay?!

21:39.350 --> 21:40.200
Password

21:39.350 --> 21:40.200
Confirmed

21:43.570 --> 21:46.160
There's no time. You can watch if you want.

21:54.630 --> 21:55.840
What?!

21:57.300 --> 21:59.210
Ruri, are you getting this?

21:59.750 --> 22:00.760
Ms. Ryoko...

22:00.760 --> 22:02.400
What the hell is this?

22:02.400 --> 22:04.230
Ms. Ryoko, please calm down.

22:04.230 --> 22:05.730
What is that?

22:05.730 --> 22:06.680
Ms. Ryoko...

22:06.680 --> 22:08.340
What the hell is this?!

22:08.340 --> 22:09.260
Ms. Ryoko!

22:13.640 --> 22:16.030
Its shape may have changed,
but nevertheless it's the Ruin.

22:16.600 --> 22:21.060
The ruin on Mars that Earth and Jupiter
were fighting over in the last war.

22:21.860 --> 22:24.240
The black box in boson jump technology.

22:24.780 --> 22:27.440
So this was at the heart of the Hisago Plan.

22:27.990 --> 22:28.900
That's right.

22:29.780 --> 22:30.920
Ruri...

22:30.920 --> 22:31.460
Yes?

22:32.120 --> 22:34.580
They must be turning in their graves!

22:34.950 --> 22:35.950
Ms. Ryoko...

22:36.910 --> 22:39.660
What the hell is this thing doing here?!

22:41.750 --> 22:44.390
For the sake of mankind's future!

22:44.390 --> 22:45.390
What?!

22:45.840 --> 22:47.310
Vice Admiral Kusakabe?

22:47.600 --> 22:49.100
Ryoko-chan, hard right!

22:54.650 --> 22:58.490
The Hisago Plan is now the domain
of the Martian Successors!

23:03.810 --> 23:05.830
We are sorry to do this directly
after occupying your ship.

23:05.830 --> 23:07.760
We will now...

23:07.760 --> 23:09.540
...destroy and abandon Amaterasu.

23:10.320 --> 23:12.790
Everyone, regardless of enemy,
friend, or civilian,

23:11.990 --> 23:14.670
Conscientious people, aren't they?

23:12.780 --> 23:15.290
evacuate immediately from this space.

23:14.660 --> 23:16.170
Did you get the data?

23:15.280 --> 23:16.960
I repeat...

23:16.160 --> 23:16.950
Oh, yes!

23:19.910 --> 23:21.880
Are you all right, Ms. Ryoko?

23:22.420 --> 23:24.670
Things aren't looking so good.

23:25.000 --> 23:26.310
Can you move?

23:26.310 --> 23:27.590
Too close...

23:28.050 --> 23:29.300
Damn it!

23:37.680 --> 23:40.310
This has nothing to do with you.
Run now!

23:40.310 --> 23:41.640
That's what I'm doing now.

23:42.520 --> 23:43.150
What the hell?

23:57.410 --> 23:58.830
Between dusk and dawn,

23:59.410 --> 24:02.090
a starry spiral stretches,
shaped just like a gourd,

24:02.090 --> 24:04.930
reaching the heavens above,
Amatsukuni beckons.

24:07.040 --> 24:09.000
Do you wish to die in front of your woman?

24:10.380 --> 24:11.210
Woman?!

24:31.480 --> 24:32.290
EVACUATION
COMPLETE

24:32.750 --> 24:34.910
Akito! It's you, isn't it?!

24:34.910 --> 24:36.360
That's why you called me
Ryoko-chan, right?!

24:36.360 --> 24:36.960
Hey!

24:37.450 --> 24:38.030
Vanish.

24:41.380 --> 24:43.880
Long time no see, and here I am!

24:49.170 --> 24:51.270
No! Go back!

24:51.270 --> 24:52.940
Yurika and Akito are...

24:52.940 --> 24:55.260
I'm sorry, Captain's orders.

24:55.800 --> 24:56.730
Ruri!

24:56.730 --> 24:58.200
Come in, damn it!

24:58.200 --> 24:59.220
You can hear me!

24:59.220 --> 25:00.600
You saw what I saw!

25:00.600 --> 25:02.090
Those two are alive!

25:02.090 --> 25:03.890
They're alive, Ruri!

25:04.270 --> 25:05.940
We're going leave them out in the cold again?

25:05.940 --> 25:07.770
Damn it! Damn it!

25:08.730 --> 25:10.420
All hands stand down.

25:10.420 --> 25:13.820
We will leave this sector as soon as we
have retrieved the Takasugi Aestivalis.

25:13.820 --> 25:14.660
Aye, aye.

25:21.370 --> 25:22.460
Haruki Kusakabe...

25:22.840 --> 25:24.210
Former Jovian Federation Vice-Admiral.

25:24.450 --> 25:27.340
The de facto number one of the
Jovian Federation during the war.

25:27.790 --> 25:30.350
The young anti-Kusakabe officers
launched a hot blooded coup d'etat.

25:30.350 --> 25:32.720
When this broke out, he was in
the forefront of fighting,

25:32.720 --> 25:35.060
and he supposedly went missing
during the combat, but...

25:35.060 --> 25:36.600
Seems he was still alive.

25:38.390 --> 25:40.140
As a former member of the Jovian Federation,

25:40.140 --> 25:41.680
I really feel sorry about this.

25:41.680 --> 25:42.910
Please, please...

25:42.910 --> 25:45.100
According to the data brought
back by Commander Hoshino,

25:45.100 --> 25:47.030
many are supporting Kusakabe's cause.

25:47.310 --> 25:49.600
Numerous military officers,
politicians, and others,

25:49.600 --> 25:51.730
all strongly tied to the
development of the Hisago Plan,

25:51.730 --> 25:52.990
are considered to be in his camp.

25:53.530 --> 25:56.360
In other words,
the United Earth ended up preparing...

25:56.360 --> 26:00.880
...the Hisago Plan just so
Kusakabe could use it to his end.

26:00.880 --> 26:01.210
Yes.

26:02.160 --> 26:05.120
At the core is the Crimson Group,
who initiated the Hisago Plan...

26:05.120 --> 26:08.230
Ruri, you need not stand to respond.

26:08.230 --> 26:09.170
Yes, Sir.

26:10.540 --> 26:13.300
It appears the confederacy of
anti-Nergal industries and Kusakabe...

26:13.300 --> 26:15.880
...were already in contact with
one another during the war.

26:16.340 --> 26:18.930
Their objective is the total
domination of boson jumping,

26:18.930 --> 26:20.650
as well as the economy and government.

26:21.050 --> 26:23.680
In the past, Admiral Kusakabe
constantly stressed...

26:23.680 --> 26:27.070
...the dangers and importance of boson jumping.

26:27.070 --> 26:29.270
He may feel that he is carrying out a just cause,

26:29.270 --> 26:31.270
but I don't think subjugated
people will see it that way.

26:31.270 --> 26:32.230
I agree.

26:32.230 --> 26:33.160
Akiyama...

26:33.940 --> 26:34.620
Yes, Sir?

26:34.880 --> 26:36.810
What kind of a man is Kusakabe?

26:36.810 --> 26:38.720
How did he appear to you?

26:38.720 --> 26:42.080
You were his direct subordinate for some time.

26:43.280 --> 26:45.740
A hot-blooded man who was second to
none in his devotion to righteousness.

26:45.740 --> 26:48.050
A man who could die to realize his ideals.

26:48.460 --> 26:51.120
But the problem was that he was a
man who believed wholeheartedly...

26:51.120 --> 26:55.010
...that righteousness in his eyes would be
righteousness in the eyes of others.

26:58.420 --> 26:59.930
Nadesico C?

27:00.340 --> 27:02.900
That's right, the third generation of Nadesico.

27:02.900 --> 27:04.650
C as in A, B, and C.

27:05.350 --> 27:08.600
It's currently going through final checking
procedures in the Nergal dock on the Moon.

27:08.980 --> 27:12.520
We would like to assign you the top
secret mission of retaking the Ruin,

27:12.520 --> 27:14.070
as an independent Nadesico force.

27:14.400 --> 27:18.190
If so, we should not recruit any regular
enlisted crew for this mission.

27:18.190 --> 27:19.190
Exactly!

27:19.610 --> 27:20.860
What are we going to do?

27:22.360 --> 27:24.140
Leave all the details to me!

27:24.140 --> 27:24.870
What?

27:24.870 --> 27:30.090
Hello from deep blue water!

27:30.090 --> 27:31.260
Nergal
Heavy
Industries

27:30.090 --> 27:31.260
Prospector

27:31.500 --> 27:35.430
And so we'll be cooperating
with your efforts.

27:35.430 --> 27:36.890
Prospector?

27:36.890 --> 27:38.170
Is that your real name?

27:38.170 --> 27:40.730
Oh no, it's like a pseudonym that I use.

27:40.730 --> 27:44.310
I suppose we should split up
and go get our crew.

27:44.310 --> 27:45.800
History repeats itself.

27:45.800 --> 27:48.820
I suppose this will be
a reunion of sorts, won't it?

27:48.820 --> 27:49.400
Yes.

27:49.740 --> 27:53.750
But I must say, Ms. Ruri,
it has been so long.

27:53.750 --> 27:55.400
Yes, it has been.

27:58.570 --> 28:00.400
But there are three of us.

28:00.900 --> 28:04.370
With the three of us together,
we can defeat any enemy!

28:05.330 --> 28:06.870
Hello!

28:07.950 --> 28:10.620
Oh wow, it's been awhile, Ruri-Ruri!

28:13.870 --> 28:17.300
The real thing!
The actual original pages of artwork!

28:14.370 --> 28:15.670
Nadesico C?

28:15.670 --> 28:18.850
Yes, since this operation is top secret,

28:17.290 --> 28:19.560
Professionals are really something
when it comes to inking!

28:18.840 --> 28:21.820
we can't have any regular enlisted
people involved, so that's why...

28:21.820 --> 28:22.970
Well...

28:24.380 --> 28:25.260
Okay.

28:26.340 --> 28:27.970
That was a quick response.

28:27.970 --> 28:30.310
Don't you have a serial to manage?

28:34.110 --> 28:36.190
Oh, you don't know just
how perfect your timing is!

28:36.190 --> 28:38.980
The deadline's tonight and I was in
a real bind with my assistants...

28:38.980 --> 28:41.140
...suddenly getting sick and going to parties.

28:41.140 --> 28:42.540
Ah, I see.

28:45.280 --> 28:47.120
Oh great, no visual again.

28:47.120 --> 28:48.580
How are you doing, Ms. Amano?

28:48.580 --> 28:50.990
Hello, who is this? I'm Hari.

28:50.990 --> 28:53.710
Huh? Ms. Amano? What's wrong, Ms. Amano?

28:53.710 --> 28:56.170
I'm small so I don't understand. Bye.

28:56.170 --> 28:57.670
Ms. Amano?! Ms. Amano?!

28:57.670 --> 28:58.840
Ms. Amano!

28:59.960 --> 29:01.170
God, what am I doing...?

29:01.170 --> 29:03.470
Hey, that's fine. Just right.
Keep it up like that!

29:03.920 --> 29:06.630
Ruri-Ruri, use 61 and
double layer for shadows, okay?

29:06.630 --> 29:06.940
Yes...

29:07.300 --> 29:09.470
Sabu-chan, make that dot rendering radiate love.

29:09.470 --> 29:10.400
I gotcha.

29:10.400 --> 29:12.890
Hari, make that curry mega-spicy, okay?

29:12.890 --> 29:13.860
Yes, Ma'am...

29:13.860 --> 29:16.820
What's impossible alone can
become possible with four!

29:16.820 --> 29:19.770
All right! Only another twelve pages to go!

29:26.210 --> 29:28.420
Oh please, come right in!

29:29.380 --> 29:31.620
Yo-chan, are you happy? Happy?

29:31.620 --> 29:34.800
Oh yeah, oh yeah. I'm really happy.

29:32.830 --> 29:34.800
Bar Kemeko

29:38.470 --> 29:42.070
One step, second step, third step...

29:42.070 --> 29:45.220
Please take me with you on your walk.

29:45.470 --> 29:48.760
No I can't Pochi, because you're a dog.

29:49.340 --> 29:52.000
And you'll get hit by a stick.

29:52.000 --> 29:55.620
Make money off of getting hit?
No, that's a bat.

29:55.620 --> 29:59.050
What you put in your brassier?
No, that's a pad.

29:59.050 --> 30:08.250
Hit it big with a job, hit it off with shopping...

30:00.940 --> 30:02.610
Are you an acquaintance of our madam?

30:04.110 --> 30:05.940
We fought in the war together.

30:08.740 --> 30:12.710
Money gets around in this world,

30:12.980 --> 30:18.540
so enjoy life while you still can...

30:24.300 --> 30:27.640
Ruri Hoshino, systems operator.
I'm eleven years old.

30:28.300 --> 30:29.300
Nice to meet you.

30:29.930 --> 30:30.750
Nice to meet you!

30:30.750 --> 30:31.180
Nice to meet you.

30:31.180 --> 30:33.720
Nice to meet you.
Nice to meet you.

30:33.720 --> 30:35.650
Ruri-chan, nice to meet you!

30:35.650 --> 30:37.270
Oh wow, you're adorable!

30:37.270 --> 30:38.770
Let's be friends, okay?

30:39.490 --> 30:42.110
The Nadesico will head to Mars!

30:42.620 --> 30:44.370
Akito, Akito!

30:44.370 --> 30:45.870
Oh, listen to me, Akito!

30:50.110 --> 30:53.450
Boson jumping is reverse engineered
technology based purely...

30:53.450 --> 30:57.090
...on what Earth and the Jovian
Federation have unearthed on Mars.

30:57.090 --> 30:59.910
For now, who finds the right Ruin
first and excavates it means more...

30:59.910 --> 31:02.800
...to the outcome of the war than
technological innovation and such.

31:03.220 --> 31:04.930
Is that all there is to it?

31:05.590 --> 31:06.390
I suppose it is.

31:06.920 --> 31:09.720
But if that search leads to a
discovery of something...

31:09.720 --> 31:11.810
...that can impact the existence
of space itself, then...

31:18.470 --> 31:19.360
SHUTTLE CRASH

31:20.480 --> 31:21.450
Professor Inez Fressange (aged 30) is
now missing following an aircraft accident.
Presumed dead.

31:47.300 --> 31:49.390
Oh, mama! You're looking good!

31:49.390 --> 31:51.220
Where are you headed?

31:51.220 --> 31:52.010
Wanna ride?

31:52.010 --> 31:53.350
Maybe next time!

31:54.050 --> 31:55.810
Oh, excuse me!

31:55.800 --> 31:56.770
Haruka

31:56.110 --> 31:57.360
I'm home!

31:57.360 --> 31:58.990
I did it, Ms. Minato!

31:58.990 --> 32:01.030
I've been selected to become a junior member!

32:01.030 --> 32:01.990
What?

32:01.990 --> 32:03.690
I'm sorry. Something's come up.

32:03.690 --> 32:05.950
I'll be out for awhile. Bye!

32:06.400 --> 32:08.080
I'm sorry. Something's come up.

32:07.480 --> 32:09.040
Why throw a kiss?

32:08.070 --> 32:10.330
I'll be out for awhile. Bye!

32:10.330 --> 32:11.610
Something's fishy...

32:12.200 --> 32:13.670
Don't you think so too?

32:15.990 --> 32:17.130
I must say...

32:17.910 --> 32:19.660
It appears the United Earth and the UEAF...

32:19.660 --> 32:21.860
...are in disarray thanks to this development.

32:21.860 --> 32:23.330
It's not too surprising.

32:23.330 --> 32:24.870
So, what are the perpetrators up to?

32:24.870 --> 32:25.340
A-Aye, Sir.

32:26.460 --> 32:28.170
The enemy, Martian Successors,

32:28.170 --> 32:30.520
have occupied the Mars Polar Ruin site.

32:30.520 --> 32:34.190
Those sympathizing with Kusakabe's
cause are gathering there as we speak.

32:35.140 --> 32:38.860
Around thirty percent of the
Unified Forces are now on his side.

32:39.120 --> 32:41.220
It appears that the marginalized
member nations of the UE...

32:41.220 --> 32:44.020
...are moving toward unofficially
endorsing the cause.

32:44.560 --> 32:48.290
With the Space Fleet so small,
few are dropping out for Kusakabe.

32:48.290 --> 32:49.450
We were fortunate!

32:49.940 --> 32:51.340
No, we are not fortunate!

32:51.340 --> 32:53.170
They are traitors!

32:53.170 --> 32:55.530
How can you be so soft on them like this?!

32:55.950 --> 32:59.660
Well, terrorist movements like these
look courageous and noble,

32:59.660 --> 33:00.910
with their simplicity and clarity and such.

33:00.910 --> 33:01.910
Please...

33:01.910 --> 33:03.300
Commander Aoi, line from outside.

33:04.010 --> 33:06.500
Hello, Jun-chan. How are you doing?

33:08.750 --> 33:10.440
Why did you patch her through?!

33:10.440 --> 33:14.010
She indicated that she was a very
close acquaintance of you, Sir.

33:15.050 --> 33:17.010
Hey, Ms. Minato is headed your way, right?

33:17.010 --> 33:18.220
What? I can't say...

33:18.220 --> 33:19.940
Don't play stupid with me!

33:20.320 --> 33:22.390
I don't care if it's Nergal or the Space Fleet,

33:22.390 --> 33:24.040
but you're up to something, aren't you?!

33:24.040 --> 33:26.910
I'm right, aren't I?! I knew it!
You're hiding something!

33:27.270 --> 33:29.740
F-For Heaven's sake,
this is classified information.

33:29.740 --> 33:32.510
There, I knew you were hiding something!

33:32.510 --> 33:36.370
Oh please, tell me!

33:36.370 --> 33:38.370
Mr. Aoi, you're the only person I can count on!

33:38.590 --> 33:41.280
If you tell me, I'll go out with you or
do whatever else you want to do.

33:41.280 --> 33:42.620
I won't be fussy!

33:42.620 --> 33:44.380
I'll be yours truly!

33:44.620 --> 33:47.220
I-Idiot! Just listen to yourself!

33:47.920 --> 33:48.800
Hey! You over there!

33:49.540 --> 33:51.840
Aoi is quite the capable person but,

33:51.840 --> 33:53.870
he's just too nice at times.

33:53.870 --> 33:55.050
I understand.

33:55.050 --> 33:58.130
Just look at how a high school
girl has him by the nose.

33:58.130 --> 34:00.270
Hey! I've had enough of this!

34:00.640 --> 34:01.930
Summer skies above,

34:01.930 --> 34:04.680
Slow to come, wind of Spring love,
The gust engulfs Jun.

34:02.260 --> 34:06.240
Summer skies above,
Slow to come, wind of spring love,
the gust engulfss Jun.
By kou-chan

34:10.480 --> 34:11.900
Hello?!

34:14.360 --> 34:15.900
He's out right now?

34:16.650 --> 34:17.570
Yes...

34:18.570 --> 34:21.200
He's at a neighborhood meeting.

34:21.700 --> 34:24.000
Well, do you have some business with him?

34:24.660 --> 34:25.830
Well, actually...

34:25.830 --> 34:27.160
No, it's nothing.

34:27.500 --> 34:29.510
We just came by because we
were in the neighborhood.

34:30.130 --> 34:32.930
You must be excited about your new baby.

34:34.250 --> 34:34.850
NOT
PARTICIPATING

34:35.380 --> 34:37.310
That's the twentieth...

34:37.590 --> 34:40.510
Another glorious former warrior dropping out.

34:40.510 --> 34:42.050
Here's your Mars Bowl!

34:42.050 --> 34:43.540
Oh, thank you.

34:43.540 --> 34:45.390
Hari, that's enough.

34:45.810 --> 34:46.520
But...

34:46.520 --> 34:47.570
But what?

34:47.950 --> 34:50.490
Is it this important to reassemble
the old crew members?

34:50.830 --> 34:51.940
It is.

34:53.980 --> 34:56.450
What's wrong with us doing it alone?

34:56.440 --> 34:58.410
Everyday Tranquility

34:57.360 --> 34:59.870
All right, I can see how we would
need more Aestivalis pilots!

34:58.410 --> 34:59.870
Closed for
preparations

35:00.270 --> 35:02.280
But I can manage the ship's
navigation just fine alone.

35:02.280 --> 35:04.810
And Mr. Saburota can take care
of the combat C&C by himself.

35:04.810 --> 35:08.340
We're the greatest team assembled
in the United Earth Space Fleet!

35:08.710 --> 35:11.580
People who retired to their civilian
jobs have lives of their own now!

35:11.960 --> 35:14.090
Are there any real meaningful reasons
behind going through all this...

35:14.090 --> 35:15.920
...to assemble together the
all-star cast of yesterday?

35:15.920 --> 35:17.650
Hari, quit it already!

35:17.650 --> 35:19.100
Please Captain!

35:19.100 --> 35:20.710
You need to tell me.

35:20.710 --> 35:21.700
Hari!

35:21.700 --> 35:23.950
Do I come across as being that undependable?

35:23.950 --> 35:24.800
Captain?!

35:25.510 --> 35:27.230
Ms. Howmei, I'd like another please.

35:30.350 --> 35:30.740
Hari!

35:31.600 --> 35:33.770
Hey, you're gonna stick us
with your share of the tab?

35:34.110 --> 35:36.080
Can't believe the fall didn't hurt him.

35:36.610 --> 35:38.660
Sure you don't need to go after him?

35:38.660 --> 35:39.720
It's fine.

35:39.720 --> 35:40.540
Are you sure?

35:41.360 --> 35:43.740
We can't defeat the enemy on our own.

35:44.240 --> 35:46.840
I'm certain that he's well aware of that.

35:46.840 --> 35:49.540
Well, there are things that he might know,
but just can't accept.

35:50.260 --> 35:52.370
We are humans after all.

35:52.960 --> 35:54.720
I'm betting he's jealous.

35:55.250 --> 35:57.470
He's jealous about your old crew.

35:57.470 --> 35:59.550
Jealous about the old Nadesico.

36:00.590 --> 36:01.880
Jealous?

36:02.760 --> 36:04.650
Now where should I start...

36:09.270 --> 36:12.070
You're a fool, Captain. You're such a fool.

36:12.350 --> 36:16.630
A fool she may be, but I have to
go back to the lodge later.

36:16.630 --> 36:19.530
How am I going to be able to
look at them after this?

36:22.900 --> 36:24.700
Ah, you're a bold one.

36:27.620 --> 36:30.250
Oh, I didn't mean to... Well, that is...

36:30.750 --> 36:31.790
I'm sorry!

36:35.750 --> 36:36.510
What is it?

36:36.750 --> 36:39.000
Oh, you're crying.

36:39.550 --> 36:41.970
Then I guess you're in no mood to
give me directions, I suppose.

36:42.760 --> 36:44.630
Y-You can't be serious, my dear pretty maiden!

36:44.630 --> 36:45.990
Let's just move on now!

36:45.990 --> 36:48.190
I am an officer in the fleet after all.

36:48.190 --> 36:50.900
I know this neighborhood
like the back of my hand!

36:50.900 --> 36:51.790
Really?

36:51.790 --> 36:54.270
I'm looking for a restaurant named
"Everyday Tranquility."

36:54.730 --> 36:55.350
Yes...

36:55.350 --> 36:57.620
Everyday... Tranquility?

36:57.620 --> 36:58.610
What's wrong?

36:58.610 --> 37:00.340
I know the place, but...

37:00.340 --> 37:02.940
If I go back right now, I won't look so good.

37:12.160 --> 37:13.600
Do you feel better now?

37:13.600 --> 37:15.760
Yes, I'm all right now.

37:15.760 --> 37:17.040
Thank you for everything.

37:17.040 --> 37:19.100
You're being so nice to someone you've just met.

37:20.630 --> 37:22.210
Hari?

37:23.550 --> 37:25.560
Yep, I knew it.

37:26.130 --> 37:30.350
You were everywhere in the letters
that Ruri-Ruri wrote to me,

37:30.350 --> 37:31.640
so that tipped me off.

37:31.640 --> 37:32.620
Me?

37:32.620 --> 37:33.530
Yes!

37:34.140 --> 37:36.360
"I have someone who's like a brother now."

37:36.360 --> 37:38.560
"His background is similar
to mine but unlike me,"

37:38.560 --> 37:40.980
"he's a bright and well behaved boy."

37:42.440 --> 37:44.500
You were on the Nadesico?

37:44.500 --> 37:46.860
Let her pamper you, Mr. Younger Brother.

37:51.530 --> 37:53.620
Hari, let's go home.

37:54.000 --> 37:55.870
You pay your share of the tab!

37:58.540 --> 38:00.360
What do we toast to?

38:00.360 --> 38:02.920
To a long overdue reunion and to Hari.

38:05.380 --> 38:07.970
So, are you coming again?
On board the Nadesico C?

38:08.380 --> 38:09.690
Well let me see.

38:09.690 --> 38:11.640
When I first heard from Mr. Prospector,

38:11.640 --> 38:14.600
I was planning on just meeting Ruri-Ruri
again and then going back, but...

38:15.220 --> 38:17.520
Now that I've seen her, I can't bring
myself to do that anymore.

38:17.520 --> 38:18.320
I know.

38:19.020 --> 38:21.900
She's pushing it.
She's not showing it much, but...

38:22.570 --> 38:25.540
Responsibilities as Captain...
Accomplishing the mission...

38:25.540 --> 38:26.690
And the enemy is no pushover.

38:27.070 --> 38:30.790
Too bad she can't cut loose in times like this.

38:31.320 --> 38:32.660
Captain, huh?

38:47.470 --> 38:49.050
Captain...

39:15.030 --> 39:17.770
Ah, it seems she's still in a bad mood.

39:17.770 --> 39:20.830
Pleasing a princess isn't easy... Huh?

39:22.130 --> 39:25.440
Oh yes, that's Miki and the others' idea.

39:25.440 --> 39:26.380
I see...

39:26.750 --> 39:30.010
They were complaining that keeping
her unclothed was sexual harassment.

39:31.300 --> 39:32.720
Doesn't that make it even more suggestive?

39:45.650 --> 39:49.080
The Battle for Terminal Colony Number 13 - Sakuya

39:49.610 --> 39:51.250
The Unified Forces are closing their perimeter.

39:49.940 --> 39:51.240
Hold them back no matter what you do.

39:51.240 --> 39:52.540
All majin units have been lost.

39:51.240 --> 39:52.540
We need just a little more time!

39:52.950 --> 39:54.000
Reinforcements will come!

39:53.990 --> 39:55.960
Unified Forces Third Fleet Flagship Yukimachizuki

39:56.530 --> 39:58.670
The enemy's strength has
gone below fifty percent!

39:59.410 --> 40:01.430
We have suffered losses of three percent.

40:01.430 --> 40:02.420
This is going well.

40:02.750 --> 40:04.080
I've just been informed that the 5th fleet...

40:04.080 --> 40:05.730
...has managed to knock out the Kushinada.

40:05.730 --> 40:08.210
Right, time for us to urge them to surrender.

40:09.010 --> 40:09.640
What was that?!

40:09.980 --> 40:11.900
Engineering's been hit! We're under attack!

40:11.900 --> 40:12.350
What?!

40:20.770 --> 40:21.860
17 vessels sunk

40:22.310 --> 40:23.040
V!

40:23.040 --> 40:24.600
Congratulations, Professor Yamasaki.

40:26.020 --> 40:29.150
Can we call this a
spectacular success, Yamasaki?

40:29.150 --> 40:29.540
Yes.

40:30.440 --> 40:32.860
Imaging communication effectiveness
of ninety-eight percent.

40:33.200 --> 40:35.160
At this rate, the accuracy of the
jump will be high enough that the...

40:35.160 --> 40:36.990
...navigator should reach the
destination almost exactly.

40:36.990 --> 40:37.500
I see.

40:37.840 --> 40:40.590
The key to success this time was this.

40:41.920 --> 40:42.870
Ururun?

40:43.920 --> 40:46.390
Comic books for young girls and boson jumping...

40:47.000 --> 40:49.340
Let's have you explain
this to us in a clear manner.

41:02.060 --> 41:04.560
The stars glimmer as the hearts of people.

41:08.650 --> 41:09.950
Tenkawa...

41:12.440 --> 41:14.110
He's on Earth...

41:19.870 --> 41:20.800
Have I kept you long?

41:21.700 --> 41:22.250
Oh, no...

41:24.670 --> 41:29.140
Destined to become a star in space tomorrow.

41:30.340 --> 41:31.310
Ruri Hoshino

41:37.340 --> 41:38.980
Ensign Hari Makibi...

41:38.980 --> 41:39.510
Aye, Ma'am!

41:39.930 --> 41:41.270
I have a special mission for you.

41:41.640 --> 41:42.970
Tomorrow at eight in the morning,

41:42.970 --> 41:44.930
you are to conduct a long distance boson jump...

41:44.930 --> 41:46.770
...to the Nergal lunar factory.

41:46.770 --> 41:49.240
Please go through the final check
procedure of the Nadesico C.

41:49.480 --> 41:50.740
The Moon?

41:50.740 --> 41:52.320
But we can't use the Chulips.

41:52.730 --> 41:55.820
This will be a singular jump
navigated by a Class A Jumper.

41:57.030 --> 42:00.120
Movement by shuttle will leave
you vulnerable to attack,

42:00.120 --> 42:01.710
making this the safest means of getting there.

42:02.090 --> 42:03.670
I'll leave Omoikane to you.

42:06.220 --> 42:07.930
Fruit basket!

42:09.130 --> 42:11.170
Oh, yeah! I win!

42:11.590 --> 42:12.570
One more time!

42:12.570 --> 42:14.270
One more match!

42:14.270 --> 42:15.850
Sure, as many times as you like.

42:16.880 --> 42:20.430
Anyone like you who only knows
pushing is easy to defeat.

42:20.930 --> 42:23.780
Shut up! Get ready, ya bum!

42:23.780 --> 42:24.820
Why sure.

42:25.270 --> 42:26.860
Is this a good idea?

42:25.600 --> 42:28.700
I'll show you what a career soldier can really do!

42:26.850 --> 42:27.850
Yes...

42:27.850 --> 42:29.350
However talented Ms. Hikaru may be,

42:29.350 --> 42:31.330
two years is a long time to
be away from the cockpit.

42:31.330 --> 42:33.150
For the purposes of intensive short term,

42:33.150 --> 42:35.610
authentic interactive combat simulation,

42:35.610 --> 42:37.790
this game is perfect!

42:37.790 --> 42:40.290
Lychee, Lyche-ru Flashing Bright Attack!

42:42.910 --> 42:44.660
You're cutting it pretty close there.

42:44.660 --> 42:45.660
Damn it!

42:45.660 --> 42:47.670
There you go again, trying to force it.

42:49.420 --> 42:52.130
Lychee, Lyche-ru Shooting Star Kick!

42:56.460 --> 42:59.390
Still, Hikaru is amazing, isn't she?

42:56.460 --> 42:58.050
One more time!

42:58.050 --> 42:59.380
Sure, why not!

42:59.380 --> 43:00.680
This is nothing.

43:00.680 --> 43:02.610
She's still at about sixty percent
of where she used to be.

43:03.140 --> 43:06.680
We need to have them be able to fight
those monsters on an equal footing.

43:07.560 --> 43:09.690
Have you found out about their latest plans?

43:09.690 --> 43:10.070
No...

43:10.730 --> 43:12.980
But we do know that they are in Japan.

43:13.360 --> 43:15.570
We also know what their goal is.

43:17.030 --> 43:20.000
Ah, it appears the trio is back together.

43:20.700 --> 43:23.450
Gotta ketchup?

43:26.870 --> 43:28.380
Prince in black...

43:29.000 --> 43:30.000
Are you...

43:31.170 --> 43:33.710
"Are you changing into
someone I do not know?"

43:34.630 --> 43:36.300
"I am changing myself..."

43:36.880 --> 43:38.720
"I'm afraid of how I'm changing."

43:39.030 --> 43:40.500
"It's a festival day!"

43:40.500 --> 43:42.340
Oh, that's the next comic.

43:43.510 --> 43:45.510
The couple's hearts drift apart.

43:46.100 --> 43:48.020
To be continued in the September issue.

43:48.640 --> 43:50.060
I believe this has been adequate.

43:51.890 --> 43:55.870
The source of the system
outbursts stems from dreams.

43:56.320 --> 43:58.990
What we visualize is relayed
to the jump system...

43:58.990 --> 44:01.540
...via the human translator Yurika Misumaru.

44:01.540 --> 44:04.200
The dreams she is experiencing are
acting like a form of noise,

44:04.200 --> 44:06.540
bringing about the system outbursts.

44:07.700 --> 44:09.300
Step right up now!

44:10.080 --> 44:12.870
We were amplifying the input image so that...

44:12.870 --> 44:16.680
...it could override Captain Misumaru's dreams.

44:16.680 --> 44:20.260
But this time we incorporated
romantic imagery into the input.

44:21.170 --> 44:23.100
So that's the reason for Ururun.

44:23.100 --> 44:23.480
Yes...

44:24.050 --> 44:25.890
We have used the dreams of
girls to our advantage.

44:25.890 --> 44:29.140
Right now, she's dreaming about
having a date with her boyfriend,

44:29.140 --> 44:30.940
causing the imaging effectiveness to skyrocket.

44:31.360 --> 44:33.940
Truly, a victory made possible by our technology!

44:53.330 --> 44:55.920
Where do you want to go, Akito?

44:57.340 --> 44:59.050
Chichibu Mountains.

45:14.940 --> 45:16.600
Tomorrow is the day.

45:18.110 --> 45:21.370
Your accurate jump is proof, isn't it?

45:21.370 --> 45:21.870
Yes...

45:22.110 --> 45:24.150
All the information we have gathered about...

45:24.150 --> 45:26.560
...the specific locations will be of aid in this.

45:26.560 --> 45:28.570
What is our mission after this?

45:28.570 --> 45:30.110
Do we just watch?

45:30.110 --> 45:34.120
No, we will merely return to our original mission.

45:34.120 --> 45:34.760
Then...

45:35.250 --> 45:37.050
The Doll and the Test Subject...

45:39.000 --> 45:40.000
Lapis...

45:44.840 --> 45:47.360
Did you sleep well last night, Ensign Makibi?

45:47.360 --> 45:48.400
I suppose...

45:48.760 --> 45:50.300
So, how did it go?

45:50.680 --> 45:51.600
What? How did what go?

45:51.600 --> 45:53.490
Oh, come on, I know all about it.

45:53.490 --> 45:55.600
You stayed with the Captain last night, right?

45:55.600 --> 45:57.060
H-How'd you know?

45:59.980 --> 46:02.620
So, was she all nice to you?

46:02.620 --> 46:04.330
Well, yes...

46:04.330 --> 46:07.070
Oh, is that so... And?

46:07.530 --> 46:09.910
I was treated to a fruity
flavored milk drink and...

46:10.660 --> 46:11.880
And then? And then?

46:12.990 --> 46:15.290
We held hands and went to sleep.

46:16.330 --> 46:17.550
Basement floor

46:21.840 --> 46:23.930
We have little time. Let's hurry.

46:23.930 --> 46:27.390
UESF Underground Jump Experimentation Dome

46:29.350 --> 46:30.870
All systems normal.

46:30.870 --> 46:33.810
Jumper's heart rate and temperature, normal.

46:34.270 --> 46:36.640
How do you feel, Ensign Makibi?

46:37.280 --> 46:40.690
Well... I feel like I've been
made into a stringed puppet.

46:42.690 --> 46:45.440
That's all there so we can
monitor your physical and...

46:45.440 --> 46:47.650
...psychological conditions
right up to when you jump.

46:47.990 --> 46:49.180
Please bear with it.

46:49.180 --> 46:49.860
Right.

46:50.450 --> 46:52.210
Hari, see you on the Moon!

46:52.660 --> 46:53.950
Okay!

46:54.290 --> 46:56.980
The navigator has entered into
the center of the circle.

46:56.980 --> 46:58.670
Beginning activation of crystals.

46:59.210 --> 47:01.210
I'm Hari Makibi. Nice to meet you.

47:01.540 --> 47:02.720
Nice to meet you.

47:02.720 --> 47:06.630
Um... This is the first time
I've met a Class A Jumper.

47:07.130 --> 47:10.610
I see. I will be conducting the
visualization of the destination.

47:10.610 --> 47:13.300
You just close your eyes and breathe easy.

47:13.300 --> 47:17.180
Think of something fun or happy or
anything else that will help you relax.

47:17.930 --> 47:19.560
Relax, relax...

47:22.020 --> 47:24.490
Activation of the Chulip Crystals
is progressing normally.

47:24.490 --> 47:27.210
Increasing levels of photons,
gravitons, and pi mesons.

47:27.210 --> 47:29.860
Synchronization of Jumper and
Navigator progressing normally.

47:30.570 --> 47:32.500
Boson exchange ratio increasing!

47:32.500 --> 47:33.780
All right, get out there!

47:36.240 --> 47:37.620
Let's go, Makibi.

47:38.160 --> 47:38.710
Yes!

47:46.920 --> 47:47.640
What's up?

47:48.260 --> 47:49.590
The princess moved.

47:50.010 --> 47:51.100
Get real.

47:51.680 --> 47:53.410
Maybe someone just boson jumped somewhere.

47:53.410 --> 47:55.100
You're just seeing things.

47:57.430 --> 47:58.430
What is it?

47:58.890 --> 48:02.190
Hari should have jumped to the Moon by now.

48:03.560 --> 48:06.540
I said you should go see him off.

48:06.540 --> 48:08.280
Not for a third time.

48:09.360 --> 48:12.610
I know it's unscientific,
but I don't want the luck to change.

48:14.370 --> 48:15.460
You're just stubborn.

48:26.460 --> 48:28.420
Akito?

48:29.260 --> 48:32.340
Today is the second anniversary.

48:40.020 --> 48:41.980
I should have realized sooner.

48:43.520 --> 48:46.810
There were many others who
either died or disappeared,

48:46.810 --> 48:50.660
besides Mr. Akito, the Captain,
and Ms. Inez back then.

48:52.150 --> 48:54.280
Class A Boson Jumpers...

48:54.610 --> 48:59.630
Navigators who can accurately communicate
to the Ruin where they want to jump to.

49:00.040 --> 49:04.220
They were all abducted by the
Martian Successors, weren't they?

49:05.920 --> 49:07.010
Abducted?

49:07.010 --> 49:12.470
Mr. Akito, I have no idea what you
went through these last two years.

49:12.470 --> 49:14.340
It's better if you don't know.

49:15.470 --> 49:18.220
I don't want to know either, but...

49:20.010 --> 49:20.940
Why?

49:21.680 --> 49:25.230
Why couldn't you tell me that you were still alive?

49:30.270 --> 49:32.530
Because there was no reason to tell you.

49:34.150 --> 49:35.150
I see.

49:37.780 --> 49:39.880
How could you say such a thing?!

49:40.410 --> 49:43.420
Aren't you the same person who said you
wanted to take Ruri into your home?

49:44.080 --> 49:45.760
Apologize, Akito!

49:45.760 --> 49:46.590
Apologize now!

49:47.010 --> 49:50.010
Ruri's been worried to death about you!

49:52.250 --> 49:53.510
Akito...?

49:57.090 --> 49:59.440
You are lax, Akito Tenkawa.

50:00.010 --> 50:02.180
You'll be coming with us.

50:03.180 --> 50:04.680
W... Who is that?

50:11.440 --> 50:14.150
I say again, come now!

50:15.440 --> 50:16.620
Akito...

50:16.950 --> 50:18.830
I don't mind if you sever one of his limbs.

50:20.290 --> 50:21.290
Slice!

50:22.160 --> 50:24.050
This has nothing to do with you.

50:24.050 --> 50:25.080
Run now.

50:25.410 --> 50:28.120
Escape is not an option in a situation like this.

50:28.500 --> 50:29.800
I think you're right.

50:30.250 --> 50:31.230
The woman?

50:31.230 --> 50:32.350
Kill her.

50:32.350 --> 50:33.380
And the girl?

50:33.380 --> 50:34.720
Capture her.

50:35.130 --> 50:37.680
Golden eyes like that of Lapis...

50:38.300 --> 50:41.530
A white fairy created by the technology of man...

50:41.530 --> 50:45.150
It appears that the people of Earth are
infatuated with genetic alterations.

50:46.480 --> 50:48.770
Thou shall become a cornerstone to...

50:48.770 --> 50:51.620
...the glorious research being conducted
at our society's laboratory.

50:54.150 --> 50:55.700
You're the ones, aren't you?

50:55.700 --> 50:59.760
The raiders that have been going about
abducting the Class A Jumpers.

50:59.760 --> 51:00.780
Correct.

51:01.580 --> 51:04.680
We are the shadows of the Martian Successors.

51:04.680 --> 51:07.550
Vile men treading a path men should not tread!

51:07.840 --> 51:10.790
All for the glory of the new order!

51:12.750 --> 51:13.420
What?!

51:15.630 --> 51:18.230
Talk of a new order is truly laughable.

51:19.050 --> 51:23.450
It is true that new order only comes
after destruction and chaos.

51:23.450 --> 51:26.420
It is natural that birth is
accompanied by so much pain.

51:26.420 --> 51:29.150
But Kusakabe has no virtue.

51:29.980 --> 51:32.570
It's been a long time, Gen-Ichiro Tsukiomi.

51:33.060 --> 51:36.370
Just listen to the barking of
the traitor that sold out Jupiter.

51:36.860 --> 51:40.420
Correct. Traitor to a friend...
Traitor to Jupiter...

51:40.420 --> 51:42.700
And now I am but a dog of Nergal.

51:44.870 --> 51:45.640
Sir!

51:45.640 --> 51:46.550
Calm yourself.

51:46.990 --> 51:50.470
It appears your attachment to Tenkawa
will be your demise, Hokushin!

51:53.960 --> 51:55.890
It's been a while, Minato.

51:56.130 --> 51:57.460
I... I guess so.

51:58.340 --> 52:01.470
This is a place reserved for
the dead to rest peacefully.

52:01.840 --> 52:03.350
Surrender yourselves quietly.

52:04.220 --> 52:05.560
If I don't?

52:06.180 --> 52:07.520
Hell will be your new home.

52:08.060 --> 52:09.230
We'll see about that.

52:09.730 --> 52:10.560
Re'puu!

52:10.560 --> 52:11.190
Right!

52:18.740 --> 52:22.700
Jovian Federation style swordsmanship
is not an assassin's skill.

52:28.000 --> 52:29.540
No way!

52:30.200 --> 52:32.000
Jovian Federation style martial arts...

52:32.920 --> 52:37.040
No sword of wickedness can
defeat my martial arts.

52:37.630 --> 52:39.390
Surrender, Hokushin!

52:40.260 --> 52:41.340
Leap!

52:43.550 --> 52:44.220
What?!

52:44.760 --> 52:45.690
Boson jump?!

52:48.510 --> 52:51.100
Akito Tenkawa, we'll meet again.

52:53.270 --> 52:55.700
Independent... boson jumping?

52:53.940 --> 52:55.690
Team A, remain in alert positions.

52:55.690 --> 52:58.580
Yurika has fallen under their spell.

52:55.700 --> 52:57.980
Everyone else, scatter and depart.

52:57.980 --> 52:58.580
Yes, Sir!

52:58.900 --> 52:59.530
What?

53:00.280 --> 53:03.070
Kusakabe's big offensive will come soon, so...

53:03.820 --> 53:04.540
So?

53:05.110 --> 53:07.880
I have something I'd like you to have.

53:09.340 --> 53:11.300
New Tokyo Bayside International Airport Spacecraft Runway B

53:12.120 --> 53:14.760
Hey everyone, it's been quite a while!

53:14.760 --> 53:17.800
We'll cover for crew chief
Uribatake's absence, right?!

53:15.000 --> 53:16.460
I'm sure you realize this,

53:16.460 --> 53:17.790
But let me just make it clear again.

53:17.790 --> 53:19.880
Time to show 'em the spirit of
the maintenance crew!!

53:17.790 --> 53:19.880
Nergal Chairman Nagare Akatsuki...

53:19.880 --> 53:21.630
Onward maintenance crew!

53:19.880 --> 53:21.630
...is counting on you on this mission.

53:21.630 --> 53:22.090
Later!

53:22.730 --> 53:24.890
Simply stated, the itinerary
consists of using...

53:23.090 --> 53:25.140
Seems like Akatsuki's luck is waning.

53:24.880 --> 53:27.270
...the jet propulsion powered mother-ship
to reach very high altitude.

53:25.130 --> 53:26.760
Doesn't have much of a presence anymore.

53:26.760 --> 53:28.400
Akatsuki's losing his hair...

53:27.260 --> 53:29.060
And from there the shuttle will be
jettisoned and use its...

53:28.390 --> 53:29.730
Hanging on by a hair...

53:29.060 --> 53:30.690
...rocket motor to go beyond the stratosphere.

53:30.690 --> 53:32.780
The ETA to the Moon will be 1400
hours standard Japan time.

53:32.780 --> 53:33.520
That is all.

53:34.480 --> 53:35.440
Ruri-Ruri?

53:35.850 --> 53:36.610
Yes?

53:36.610 --> 53:39.690
What did Akito give you?

53:40.270 --> 53:41.700
It's a recipe.

53:41.700 --> 53:42.580
A recipe?

53:42.960 --> 53:45.200
The Tenkawa Special Ramen recipe.

53:45.570 --> 53:47.780
Oh, the one he offered out of his street cart.

53:47.780 --> 53:48.620
Yes...

53:51.410 --> 53:54.010
I can't accept this from you!

53:54.540 --> 53:59.350
This is something that you'll need
after you've rescued Ms. Yurika.

53:59.350 --> 54:00.970
I have no use for it anymore.

54:01.380 --> 54:04.180
The Akito Tenkawa that you knew is dead.

54:05.050 --> 54:07.680
I would like you to keep it
as proof of his existence.

54:07.680 --> 54:09.830
You're being a showoff.

54:09.830 --> 54:11.430
You don't understand, Ruri-chan.

54:12.560 --> 54:16.070
They messed around with my brain while
they were experimenting on me.

54:16.360 --> 54:17.770
Ever since then...

54:21.360 --> 54:23.120
My sense of taste, you see,

54:23.120 --> 54:23.950
is no good any longer.

54:24.340 --> 54:27.240
When I get excited, it all shines up.

54:27.610 --> 54:28.420
It's like a comic book, isn't it?

54:29.200 --> 54:32.790
I won't be able to make ramen for you anymore.

54:37.210 --> 54:40.920
Look forward to the victory
celebration we'll be preparing!

54:42.040 --> 54:45.260
Strange how we're on the side,
seeing them off.

54:46.840 --> 54:48.270
Mr. Pros!

54:48.550 --> 54:50.140
Ms. Howmei!

54:50.140 --> 54:51.230
Hello!

54:51.230 --> 54:54.350
Well, well. But they've already taken off.

54:54.350 --> 54:57.100
No, they have a different mission to work on.

54:57.100 --> 54:57.730
Another...?

54:57.730 --> 54:59.700
Okay, everyone, time for us to go.

54:59.700 --> 55:00.690
Yes, Sir!

55:07.400 --> 55:09.860
Please sit back and enjoy the flight now.

55:11.950 --> 55:14.290
Would you like some beverages?

55:16.370 --> 55:20.920
We have juices, colas, beers, whiskey,
and beer snacks as well!

55:22.210 --> 55:23.540
The beautiful legs!

55:23.880 --> 55:25.740
Hey, hey, wait a minute, Yukina!

55:25.740 --> 55:28.140
What the heck are you doing here?!

55:28.360 --> 55:30.320
I'd like some hiyashi ame.

55:30.320 --> 55:31.310
Right up!

55:31.310 --> 55:33.400
Durian juice.

55:32.140 --> 55:34.110
We have more important business to deal with!

55:34.420 --> 55:37.610
You've got school!
You should go home right now!

55:37.610 --> 55:39.370
It's summer vacation now.

55:39.370 --> 55:42.230
What about track and field?!
You've got intramural races coming up!

55:42.230 --> 55:43.940
That's the week after next.

55:43.940 --> 55:47.070
And besides, if the mission fails,
they'll be called off, right?

55:47.860 --> 55:49.400
You're a fool! Go back home!

55:49.400 --> 55:51.470
Blah, blah, nag, nag...

55:51.470 --> 55:52.460
Hey, Jun!

55:52.700 --> 55:54.730
Hey, knock it off!
How did you get yourself into this?!

55:54.730 --> 55:56.880
Oh... Well... I...

55:56.880 --> 56:00.540
Nobody is going to take you seriously
when you're dressed like that.

56:00.540 --> 56:01.290
Yeah...

56:01.960 --> 56:02.930
You're so cute!

56:03.250 --> 56:04.440
Ms. Minato...

56:04.440 --> 56:08.320
Let's talk about this later,
after we reach the Moon.

56:08.320 --> 56:11.270
Oh yes, yes. Later is better.

56:11.270 --> 56:14.030
You know, you're going to get burnt
really bad one of these days.

56:14.030 --> 56:14.900
Yes, yes.

56:18.480 --> 56:20.440
Main boosters full power!

56:20.440 --> 56:22.400
5 G! 6 G!

56:25.310 --> 56:27.820
Just a little more. A little more, Izumi.

56:28.490 --> 56:30.750
What the hell are those two up to?

56:29.030 --> 56:30.760
This is... This is...

56:30.750 --> 56:35.460
Space...

56:30.760 --> 56:32.860
Supposedly they're reenacting
leaving the Earth's atmosphere...

56:32.860 --> 56:34.370
...in the style of old anime.

56:34.370 --> 56:35.450
I see...

56:36.460 --> 56:38.790
To note, shuttles in 23rd century...

56:38.790 --> 56:42.580
...are comfortable and simple,
thanks to gravity control systems!

56:42.580 --> 56:43.430
What?!

56:45.290 --> 56:47.460
We've reached stationary satellite orbit.

56:47.840 --> 56:50.850
Ah well... At least the ride so far's been...

56:50.850 --> 56:52.340
Not pleasant!

56:52.720 --> 56:54.550
What? Something go wrong?

56:55.800 --> 56:58.820
You knew that she was on board, didn't you?!

56:58.820 --> 57:01.320
Shiratori's younger sister? Yes, I did.

57:01.320 --> 57:04.860
I don't believe it! Why didn't you tell me?

57:04.850 --> 57:08.210
Because I wanted to avoid unnecessary
hassles before we took off.

57:08.210 --> 57:09.500
Unnecessary?!

57:09.500 --> 57:10.330
Just listen.

57:10.820 --> 57:13.030
That girl is the younger sister
of Shiratori Tsukumo,

57:13.030 --> 57:14.290
hero to the Jovian Federation.

57:14.990 --> 57:17.490
They might be after her as their next target.

57:17.990 --> 57:19.870
It would be more dangerous to leave her alone.

57:21.200 --> 57:23.470
Rendezvousing with our escort fleet.

57:26.880 --> 57:30.170
I'm Araragi, commander of this fleet.
It's nice to meet you.

57:30.670 --> 57:33.170
I'm Ruri Hoshino, captain of Nadesico.

57:33.550 --> 57:35.930
Nice to meet you, Sir, and thank you.

57:35.930 --> 57:38.640
No, please, escorting a fairy such as yourself...

57:38.640 --> 57:40.650
The honor of being your knight is entirely ours.

57:41.100 --> 57:43.420
The white flower which has
bloomed in blue space...

57:43.420 --> 57:45.390
Ruri Hoshino, the Cybernetic Fairy...

57:45.770 --> 57:49.190
My men refer you as the Cybernetic Fairy.

57:50.440 --> 57:51.940
You are truly a lovely sight to behold.

57:52.280 --> 57:53.610
Yes, thank you.

57:54.110 --> 57:57.740
Please send my regards to
your subordinates as well.

57:58.870 --> 58:01.760
The Cybernetic Fairy was adorable, wasn't she?

58:01.760 --> 58:03.950
Yes, truly a treasure of space.

58:03.950 --> 58:06.570
I got that visual recorded just fine, Sir!

58:06.570 --> 58:08.540
All right, we'll show it to the others later.

58:09.710 --> 58:12.130
Boson particle readings are
increasing 5000 km ahead of us!

58:12.130 --> 58:12.850
What?!

58:14.670 --> 58:16.180
Enemy convoy dead ahead!

58:17.180 --> 58:18.520
Battleship, frigate...

58:18.520 --> 58:20.020
Civilian shuttle, our target!

58:20.930 --> 58:23.430
Behold, as this surely is the
covert operations ship...

58:23.430 --> 58:25.490
...that our intelligence was speaking of!

58:25.490 --> 58:28.820
All units, ignore the battleship, get the shuttle!

58:28.820 --> 58:29.450
Aye, aye, Sir!

58:29.750 --> 58:31.590
All units, full speed ahead!

58:31.590 --> 58:33.660
Form a diamond shaped formation
to puncture through the enemy!

58:34.400 --> 58:36.110
The shuttle will accelerate ahead.

58:37.040 --> 58:40.380
Okay now, leave this to the
specialist from now on!

58:40.950 --> 58:44.210
All crew members, wear your seat belts.
Prepare for shock.

58:44.210 --> 58:45.340
All right!

58:46.120 --> 58:49.720
So you want me to shoot straight
through the enemy?

58:49.720 --> 58:52.710
Yes, just blast ahead and
let us escape them please.

58:52.710 --> 58:53.810
Aye, aye!

58:56.880 --> 58:58.440
The shuttle's on point?

58:58.440 --> 58:59.900
The fools intend to die?

59:02.980 --> 59:04.790
Field strength holding at eighty percent.

59:04.790 --> 59:05.680
We can still push it!

59:05.680 --> 59:07.310
A little more... A little more...

59:13.980 --> 59:15.870
The enemy is confused from losing its target.

59:16.490 --> 59:19.580
We will push through the enemy,
then become the shuttle's shield!

59:19.990 --> 59:22.700
To seek life in the clutches of death...
She's a remarkable fairy.

59:23.780 --> 59:26.180
Boson readings originating
ahead of the shuttle's heading.

59:26.180 --> 59:26.760
What?!

59:28.710 --> 59:30.330
Not good. We'll be flanked at this rate.

59:30.330 --> 59:32.680
This is not what I bargained for!

59:33.430 --> 59:34.140
Situation Prediction

59:33.430 --> 59:34.140
Being flanked and suffering a

59:33.430 --> 59:34.140
BRUTAL BEATING

59:34.380 --> 59:36.140
Don't you have any armaments?

59:36.140 --> 59:38.090
We took them off in the process of camouflaging.

59:38.090 --> 59:39.380
Had to be thorough, I see.

59:40.930 --> 59:43.560
Undoubtedly this is a mutiny on a cosmic scale!

59:43.980 --> 59:48.940
In the eyes of the United Earth Charter,
this is a clear threat to peace!

59:49.690 --> 59:51.150
We are evil.

59:51.690 --> 59:55.080
However, space-time transference
ushers in a dawn to a new world,

59:55.080 --> 59:57.990
a new canon of order!

59:58.320 --> 01:00:00.960
Now, light the way for our heroes!

01:00:02.950 --> 01:00:03.670
Visualizing!

01:00:03.670 --> 01:00:04.420
Visualizing!

01:00:04.420 --> 01:00:05.280
Visualizing!

01:00:10.210 --> 01:00:12.380
Destination!
United Earth Headquarters Building!

01:00:12.680 --> 01:00:14.550
Destination!
Unified Forces GHQ Building!

01:00:15.420 --> 01:00:17.210
Navigators, continuing with visualization!

01:00:17.630 --> 01:00:19.770
Image transfer rate at fifty percent.

01:00:20.300 --> 01:00:22.720
Initiate transfer enhancement program.

01:00:23.090 --> 01:00:24.420
Run in multi-mode.

01:00:24.420 --> 01:00:25.730
Multi-mode input.

01:00:37.440 --> 01:00:38.740
Akito!

01:00:39.610 --> 01:00:41.870
Where do you want to go, Akito?

01:00:45.000 --> 01:00:46.710
Not so fast, cuties.

01:00:55.090 --> 01:00:57.510
What are those two up to?

01:00:55.540 --> 01:00:56.750
Sudden acceleration!

01:00:56.750 --> 01:00:57.500
Gee...

01:00:57.500 --> 01:00:59.560
Supposedly they're reenacting
high stress acceleration G...

01:00:57.880 --> 01:00:59.550
Another burst!

01:00:59.550 --> 01:01:01.020
...in the style of old anime.

01:00:59.550 --> 01:01:01.040
Gee...

01:01:01.040 --> 01:01:03.560
Amazing how those pilots
can have fun at a time like this.

01:01:01.970 --> 01:01:03.560
One more for luck!

01:01:05.260 --> 01:01:07.260
Boson reactions from 50km ahead!

01:01:07.260 --> 01:01:07.810
What?!

01:01:11.270 --> 01:01:12.390
This one's big!

01:01:12.390 --> 01:01:14.600
Whoa, trouble to the power of two.

01:01:15.480 --> 01:01:17.660
Firing gravity blast cannon!

01:01:33.410 --> 01:01:35.340
Emergency leap! Run!

01:01:37.790 --> 01:01:40.140
Captain, Ms. Minato, did you see that?!

01:01:42.760 --> 01:01:44.220
C... Crew chief?

01:01:44.220 --> 01:01:46.270
Hey, all of you, how are ya?

01:01:46.270 --> 01:01:48.580
Mr. Seiya, why are you there?

01:01:48.580 --> 01:01:50.890
You know, "I thought this might happen, so..."

01:01:50.890 --> 01:01:52.730
Glad I made it out here before you did.

01:01:52.730 --> 01:01:54.990
You can laugh this off as
being a convenient plot twist!

01:01:54.990 --> 01:01:58.320
But behold! Behold how this
is such a cool development!

01:01:58.320 --> 01:02:00.160
And behold this technology!

01:02:00.690 --> 01:02:05.580
Ain't no way you can keep a mechanic
from all this mysterious new technology!

01:02:01.400 --> 01:02:03.110
Those scars on his face,

01:02:03.110 --> 01:02:04.610
his wife must have made them.

01:02:04.990 --> 01:02:07.120
The price of a convenient plot twist, I guess.

01:02:07.460 --> 01:02:10.590
In any case, Mr. Seiya, Hari, I'd like to know.

01:02:11.910 --> 01:02:14.160
How did you boson jump?

01:02:14.540 --> 01:02:16.330
A convenient plot twist, yes, but...

01:02:18.250 --> 01:02:19.550
Let me explain!

01:02:23.130 --> 01:02:25.390
Yes, they arrived from nowhere and...

01:02:29.680 --> 01:02:31.680
International High Speed
Communications, occupied!

01:02:33.350 --> 01:02:35.200
Sir, we're almost done...

01:02:35.200 --> 01:02:38.350
Yes, a new order will come into being.

01:02:40.320 --> 01:02:42.820
3, 2, 1...

01:02:43.320 --> 01:02:44.410
"Kaboom!"

01:02:46.070 --> 01:02:48.040
Get to
Know the

01:02:46.070 --> 01:02:48.040
Nadesico!

01:02:46.070 --> 01:02:48.040
The Motion
Picture Edition

01:02:46.280 --> 01:02:48.040
Get to Know the Nadesico!

01:02:48.530 --> 01:02:50.990
Hello, it's been awhile. Nice to meet you.

01:02:51.370 --> 01:02:55.460
I'm Inez Fressange, medical and science
crew officer for the Nadesico.

01:02:56.200 --> 01:02:58.120
Control over politics, economics,

01:02:58.120 --> 01:03:00.170
entertainment, morality and chastity...

01:03:00.170 --> 01:03:02.090
...in the new order ushered in with the arrival...

01:03:02.090 --> 01:03:04.650
...of the era of boson jumping,
is their true goal.

01:03:04.650 --> 01:03:07.170
So how would boson jumping change the world?

01:03:07.170 --> 01:03:07.980
Question.

01:03:08.350 --> 01:03:09.510
Yes, Ruri-chan?

01:03:09.840 --> 01:03:12.560
I believe everyone has the same
question burning inside.

01:03:12.860 --> 01:03:16.180
Didn't you die, Ms. Inez?

01:03:16.560 --> 01:03:18.830
Y-Yeah, that's right! Why are you alive?!

01:03:18.830 --> 01:03:21.410
W... Why am I alive? How rude. All right.

01:03:22.150 --> 01:03:23.920
This time I'll explain.

01:03:23.920 --> 01:03:25.610
Hey, it's the washed up womanizer.

01:03:26.860 --> 01:03:28.210
Ouch, that hurts.

01:03:28.210 --> 01:03:29.660
Then there are people out there making noise...

01:03:29.660 --> 01:03:31.740
...about how I'm a Class A war criminal
and all sorts of other gossip.

01:03:31.740 --> 01:03:33.370
We don't care a rat's ass about any of that!

01:03:33.700 --> 01:03:35.670
Just hurry up and explain what's going on!

01:03:35.670 --> 01:03:38.460
Hey, Ryoko, weren't you in the Unified Forces?

01:03:38.790 --> 01:03:40.670
Who cares about details like that!

01:03:42.210 --> 01:03:44.500
In any case, to trick the enemy,

01:03:44.500 --> 01:03:46.570
sometimes you need to trick
your friends, you know.

01:03:46.570 --> 01:03:50.180
See, since Tenkawa and the
Captain were abducted,

01:03:50.180 --> 01:03:54.220
having her officially listed as dead was
the most effective step we could take.

01:03:54.890 --> 01:03:57.000
Can I ask you a question?

01:03:57.000 --> 01:03:57.530
Yes?

01:03:57.830 --> 01:04:01.770
Mr. Akatsuki, are you a bad guy or a good guy?

01:04:02.940 --> 01:04:04.810
You get straight to the point, don't you?

01:04:04.810 --> 01:04:06.610
Oops, I have a call on the other line.

01:04:06.610 --> 01:04:07.190
See ya!

01:04:08.110 --> 01:04:10.040
Oh boy. This really is something.

01:04:08.120 --> 01:04:11.320
This is the front gate! The enemy
offensive has been persistent...

01:04:11.320 --> 01:04:13.720
It's all right. Leave the rest up to me now.

01:04:13.720 --> 01:04:14.240
Yes, Sir!

01:04:14.660 --> 01:04:16.870
Right! The stage has been set.

01:04:17.240 --> 01:04:18.210
Time to go!

01:04:19.460 --> 01:04:22.050
United Earth General Assembly Hall

01:04:22.870 --> 01:04:24.250
Enemy guard force silent!

01:04:24.960 --> 01:04:26.250
We'll make our assault now!

01:04:33.640 --> 01:04:35.560
Well now, aren't we eager?

01:04:36.680 --> 01:04:37.520
Megu-tan...

01:04:38.060 --> 01:04:41.200
Hello everyone! I'm Megumi Reinard!

01:04:41.200 --> 01:04:42.990
We're the Howmei Girls!

01:04:43.370 --> 01:04:47.070
We'd like to extend to all of you attending
our concert, our warmest welcome.

01:04:47.820 --> 01:04:49.940
Please let yourself have a great time.

01:04:52.360 --> 01:04:53.570
The General Assembly...

01:04:53.570 --> 01:04:55.380
Where is the General Assembly of the UE?!

01:04:56.320 --> 01:04:57.450
Mr. Pros on the guitar!

01:04:57.450 --> 01:04:58.340
I don't know about this.

01:04:58.720 --> 01:05:00.500
Yoshisada Munetake on the bass.

01:05:00.500 --> 01:05:01.300
Happy!

01:05:01.590 --> 01:05:04.260
And we have Ms. Howmei
jumping in on the keyboards!

01:05:04.630 --> 01:05:05.470
All right!

01:05:05.470 --> 01:05:07.290
Hya! Hya! Hya! Hya!

01:05:07.290 --> 01:05:10.220
Drums by Kou-Ichiro Misumaru
and Genpachiro Akiyama!

01:05:10.710 --> 01:05:12.420
And our special guest!

01:05:13.010 --> 01:05:14.350
Nagare Akatsuki!

01:05:23.520 --> 01:05:25.400
Don't underestimate the stinkin' rich!

01:05:25.980 --> 01:05:27.740
Divine Retribution!

01:05:29.860 --> 01:05:31.210
Distortion Field?

01:05:31.210 --> 01:05:33.890
I told you, don't underestimate.

01:05:33.890 --> 01:05:35.950
You fiends! What is the meaning of this?!

01:05:35.950 --> 01:05:36.880
The meaning of this?

01:05:37.410 --> 01:05:39.490
It means you should stop
doing meaningless things.

01:05:39.490 --> 01:05:40.590
What?!

01:05:40.590 --> 01:05:43.690
No organization that attempts to take the
General Assembly members hostage...

01:05:43.690 --> 01:05:45.180
...will ever be able to take the world.

01:05:45.750 --> 01:05:48.000
Thou needst not die.

01:05:50.710 --> 01:05:52.420
Then we can kill you!

01:05:58.650 --> 01:06:01.770
Traitor Nagare Akatsuki! Divine Retribution!

01:06:13.320 --> 01:06:15.570
Most of the soldiers outside
have been neutralized.

01:06:15.570 --> 01:06:16.990
Give yourselves up.

01:06:17.320 --> 01:06:19.250
Boson jumping... A new model, is it?

01:06:21.370 --> 01:06:23.710
It's been sometime, Ensign Kawaguchi.

01:06:24.500 --> 01:06:25.920
Commander Tsukiomi?!

01:06:26.750 --> 01:06:29.390
I've just heard Ruri made it to the Nadesico C.

01:06:29.390 --> 01:06:30.700
It's a done deal.

01:06:30.700 --> 01:06:31.350
Yes...

01:06:32.090 --> 01:06:36.770
Once she becomes one with Omoikane's
systems, they'll be invincible.

01:06:37.050 --> 01:06:39.800
So all that data collected off
of our fighting has paid off.

01:06:40.350 --> 01:06:41.650
You're going?

01:06:41.650 --> 01:06:42.350
Yes.

01:06:43.220 --> 01:06:48.330
Revenge. It's a word that would have
been so unlike you in the past.

01:06:48.330 --> 01:06:50.490
The past is the past, now is now.

01:06:51.110 --> 01:06:52.820
Thanks for the refueling.

01:06:52.820 --> 01:06:53.730
It's nothing.

01:06:54.860 --> 01:06:58.000
I'm just on an errand from the chairman.

01:06:58.000 --> 01:07:00.380
Cancel all the hits?!

01:07:01.120 --> 01:07:02.880
What is that supposed to mean?! Explain!

01:07:02.880 --> 01:07:06.950
W... Well, sir, the enemy's
new weapons and persuasions...

01:07:06.950 --> 01:07:07.960
Persuasions?

01:07:07.960 --> 01:07:09.880
Tsukumo Shiratori must be rolling
in his grave right now.

01:07:10.110 --> 01:07:11.250
Tsukiomi?

01:07:10.140 --> 01:07:14.260
Men of courage from the former Jovian
Federation and Earth, lay down your arms.

01:07:12.250 --> 01:07:14.250
Boson reading coming from air space above us!

01:07:14.250 --> 01:07:14.880
What?!

01:07:28.140 --> 01:07:30.450
We have visual from surveillance craft.
It's the Nadesico!

01:07:30.450 --> 01:07:31.400
Nadesico?!

01:07:32.860 --> 01:07:33.280
SLEEPING

01:07:33.490 --> 01:07:33.990
TIME TO REST

01:07:36.320 --> 01:07:38.750
Hey you! Stay at your posts!

01:07:39.150 --> 01:07:41.810
It's not us! The units are moving on their own.

01:07:41.810 --> 01:07:42.740
What?!

01:07:43.040 --> 01:07:43.960
SLEEPING

01:07:44.090 --> 01:07:45.670
Losing control!

01:07:45.990 --> 01:07:47.130
Losing control!

01:07:50.750 --> 01:07:52.080
Hijacked the system?

01:07:53.290 --> 01:07:54.260
The Fairy?

01:08:00.510 --> 01:08:02.570
Phase transition engine,
no abnormalities reported.

01:08:02.570 --> 01:08:06.180
All stations please shift
to alert status pattern B.

01:08:06.850 --> 01:08:11.380
Hari, take over all of the Nadesico C's systems.

01:08:11.380 --> 01:08:13.310
What? A-All of them?!

01:08:13.650 --> 01:08:15.580
Not just the backups?

01:08:15.580 --> 01:08:21.030
Yes, I'm going to take over
all enemy systems on Mars.

01:08:21.450 --> 01:08:23.120
I can't cover the ship's systems then.

01:08:23.820 --> 01:08:26.280
Nadesico C will be all yours.

01:08:26.620 --> 01:08:27.370
But...

01:08:27.370 --> 01:08:29.200
You can do it, Hari!

01:08:30.660 --> 01:08:33.300
No more pampering. It's time to be a man.

01:08:33.300 --> 01:08:38.970
And so, Ruri took control over
all enemy units in and around Mars.

01:08:40.010 --> 01:08:41.200
She is something.

01:08:41.200 --> 01:08:43.220
How are you feeling?

01:08:43.760 --> 01:08:44.760
All right.

01:08:44.760 --> 01:08:48.600
But it's no cake walk to have to jump an
entire battleship to Mars in one leap.

01:08:48.600 --> 01:08:49.530
I'm sure.

01:08:50.060 --> 01:08:52.200
A new order...

01:08:52.980 --> 01:08:54.610
Hello, everyone.

01:08:55.400 --> 01:09:00.620
I am Ruri Hoshino, captain of
United Earth Space Fleet's Nadesico C.

01:09:01.320 --> 01:09:03.910
Former Jovian Federation
Vice-Admiral Haruki Kusakabe,

01:09:03.910 --> 01:09:05.520
I place you under arrest.

01:09:05.520 --> 01:09:06.740
Silence, vile witch!

01:09:09.080 --> 01:09:10.080
We will triumph!

01:09:11.540 --> 01:09:12.870
Fight to the bitter end!

01:09:13.920 --> 01:09:16.790
I want your word that my subordinates
will be taken care of.

01:09:23.220 --> 01:09:25.040
Seven boson readings...

01:09:25.040 --> 01:09:26.010
Ruri-Ruri!

01:09:26.430 --> 01:09:27.470
Ignore them.

01:09:28.720 --> 01:09:31.230
I'll leave them to him.

01:09:34.940 --> 01:09:36.480
Are you sure, Sir?

01:09:36.980 --> 01:09:39.580
Surprise attacks employing jumping
are a double-edged sword.

01:09:39.950 --> 01:09:43.680
With Amaterasu gone, our chances
for victory were fifty-fifty.

01:09:43.680 --> 01:09:48.330
But once a Class A Jumper was revealed
to be still alive, our chances...

01:10:04.050 --> 01:10:06.140
Time to end this.

01:10:28.490 --> 01:10:29.540
Who are you?

01:10:29.800 --> 01:10:30.830
I am Ruri.

01:10:31.160 --> 01:10:33.080
This is my friend Omoikane.

01:10:33.620 --> 01:10:34.760
And you are?

01:10:34.760 --> 01:10:35.540
Lapis.

01:10:35.960 --> 01:10:36.870
Lapis?

01:10:37.620 --> 01:10:38.790
Lapis Lazuli.

01:10:39.210 --> 01:10:41.350
I was born inside a Nergal laboratory.

01:10:41.840 --> 01:10:43.730
I am Akito's eyes,

01:10:43.730 --> 01:10:45.100
Akito's ears,

01:10:45.100 --> 01:10:46.450
Akito's hands,

01:10:46.450 --> 01:10:47.780
Akito's feet,

01:10:47.780 --> 01:10:49.840
Akito's... Akito's...

01:11:16.160 --> 01:11:18.760
I can sense your fear, your anguish.

01:11:18.760 --> 01:11:20.760
No matter how thick the armor you don,

01:11:21.080 --> 01:11:23.670
the heart's weaknesses are still exposed!

01:11:34.350 --> 01:11:35.650
Sir!

01:11:35.650 --> 01:11:36.280
What?!

01:11:37.610 --> 01:11:39.240
Here comes the cavalry!

01:11:39.530 --> 01:11:43.880
Men who interrupt a duel ought to be
kicked into the river Styx by a horse!

01:11:43.880 --> 01:11:45.540
Horse number one!

01:11:45.540 --> 01:11:47.250
The second!

01:11:47.530 --> 01:11:49.530
So, that makes me a horse too?

01:11:49.530 --> 01:11:51.460
That's right, and being a horse...

01:11:51.460 --> 01:11:53.660
Ryoko takes him for a ride.

01:11:53.660 --> 01:11:54.740
Hey, that's good.

01:11:54.740 --> 01:11:56.730
You jackasses! No one rides anyone!

01:11:56.730 --> 01:11:57.170
Oops!

01:11:57.910 --> 01:11:59.670
Well, we'll leave it up until later to find out...

01:11:59.670 --> 01:12:01.420
...if she'll ride me or I ride on her lap.

01:12:01.420 --> 01:12:02.250
Right, Lieutenant?

01:12:02.250 --> 01:12:03.090
Y-You fool!

01:12:03.090 --> 01:12:04.930
Just listen to their sweet nothings.

01:12:04.930 --> 01:12:08.350
You bastard! You just wait till after this is done!

01:12:06.000 --> 01:12:07.210
Be careful!

01:12:07.210 --> 01:12:09.350
They might be yapping,
but they're formidable foes!

01:12:09.720 --> 01:12:11.340
Damn it! I'm out!

01:12:20.480 --> 01:12:22.200
Amazing how far you've gotten.

01:12:22.200 --> 01:12:25.160
I've witnessed true persistence.

01:12:26.440 --> 01:12:27.620
We end this now.

01:12:29.900 --> 01:12:32.070
Damn it! Stop fooling around!

01:12:32.070 --> 01:12:33.700
We're fighting, we're fighting!

01:12:33.700 --> 01:12:36.370
Serious fighting. Here I fire at thee.

01:12:38.830 --> 01:12:39.910
Quick draw?

01:12:41.580 --> 01:12:42.470
How absurd!

01:12:57.430 --> 01:12:58.480
Remarkable...

01:13:29.170 --> 01:13:30.560
What? All of you?

01:13:31.710 --> 01:13:33.800
You're all so much older.

01:13:34.590 --> 01:13:36.940
Thank God, you're clueless as usual.

01:13:37.680 --> 01:13:40.350
I've been seeing this dream all this time.

01:13:41.020 --> 01:13:41.980
Akito?

01:13:42.600 --> 01:13:44.900
Where is Akito?

01:13:48.360 --> 01:13:50.830
Goodbye!

01:13:51.570 --> 01:13:53.480
Are you sure this was a good idea?

01:13:53.480 --> 01:13:56.360
You're not about to stop him
when he says he needs to go.

01:13:56.860 --> 01:14:00.740
But what's he going to do from now on?

01:14:02.330 --> 01:14:03.660
He'll be back.

01:14:04.750 --> 01:14:07.210
And if he doesn't, I'll just go after him.

01:14:08.210 --> 01:14:09.210
Ruri-Ruri?

01:14:10.960 --> 01:14:12.380
Because he's...

01:14:13.920 --> 01:14:16.190
Because he's someone precious...

01:14:16.470 --> 01:14:21.220
My revolution that went on its own.

01:14:16.470 --> 01:14:21.220
hitori aruki no my revolution

01:14:21.640 --> 01:14:24.600
After so many encounters,

01:14:21.640 --> 01:14:24.600
ikutsumono deai

01:14:24.600 --> 01:14:27.690
I've come across so much.

01:14:24.600 --> 01:14:27.690
ni mitsuketa

01:14:27.770 --> 01:14:33.780
Kindness... Sorrow...

01:14:27.770 --> 01:14:33.780
yasashisa setsunasa

01:14:37.280 --> 01:14:42.080
The canvas spread out in my heart...

01:14:37.280 --> 01:14:42.080
kokoro ni hiraku kyanbasu wa

01:14:42.490 --> 01:14:48.540
...has been bruised and soiled in places, but...

01:14:42.490 --> 01:14:48.540
kizutsuitari yogoretari demo

01:14:48.750 --> 01:14:55.590
...the vague emotions drawn on it...

01:14:48.750 --> 01:14:55.590
egakare dasareta

01:14:55.590 --> 01:14:57.930
...still show through.

01:14:55.590 --> 01:14:57.930
awai kannjyou

01:14:57.930 --> 01:15:04.640
Your voice, your hair, even if...

01:14:57.930 --> 01:15:04.640
anata no koe anata no kami moshimo

01:15:05.890 --> 01:15:10.230
...we meet again after a thousand years,

01:15:05.890 --> 01:15:10.230
sennen tatte attemo

01:15:10.230 --> 01:15:15.980
I'll still be able to tell them apart.

01:15:10.230 --> 01:15:15.980
mada oboeteiru

01:15:16.400 --> 01:15:18.780
As many as there are stars above.

01:15:16.400 --> 01:15:18.780
hoshi no kazu hodo

01:15:18.780 --> 01:15:21.320
Memories of days passed,

01:15:18.780 --> 01:15:21.320
anohi no koto

01:15:21.320 --> 01:15:25.580
of the days to come, oh please...

01:15:21.320 --> 01:15:25.580
ashita no koto motto

01:15:26.250 --> 01:15:31.460
Give them to me, for I will never...

01:15:26.250 --> 01:15:31.460
omoide kudasai watashi wa

01:15:31.460 --> 01:15:37.130
...ever be able to purge myself of you.

01:15:31.460 --> 01:15:37.130
anata wo kesenakute

01:15:37.300 --> 01:15:43.390
Forever full up my love.

01:15:50.310 --> 01:15:55.070
A generation that has been fighting all the time.

01:15:50.310 --> 01:15:55.070
tatakai tsuzuketa generation

01:15:55.610 --> 01:16:01.530
Behind the smiles, a tear-stained...

01:15:55.610 --> 01:16:01.530
egao no oku ni namida iro no

01:16:01.700 --> 01:16:08.620
...strength hides quietly,

01:16:01.700 --> 01:16:08.620
tsuyosa wo himeteru

01:16:08.620 --> 01:16:10.910
in search of something.

01:16:08.620 --> 01:16:10.910
nanika wo motome

01:16:10.910 --> 01:16:17.750
Your eyes, your fingertips...

01:16:10.910 --> 01:16:17.750
anata no me mo anata no yubisaki mo

01:16:19.050 --> 01:16:23.260
I'll be able to find them again...

01:16:19.050 --> 01:16:23.260
umare kawatte soredemo

01:16:23.260 --> 01:16:28.720
...even if they're born anew.

01:16:23.260 --> 01:16:28.720
mada sagaseruwa

01:16:29.470 --> 01:16:31.810
As many as there are stars above.

01:16:29.470 --> 01:16:31.810
hoshi no kazu hodo

01:16:31.810 --> 01:16:38.610
There are loves, there are dreams, even still...

01:16:31.810 --> 01:16:38.610
ai ga atte yume ga atte dakedo

01:16:39.230 --> 01:16:44.530
Let me adorn life with my unchanging Iove...

01:16:39.230 --> 01:16:44.530
kawaranu omoi wo kasanete

01:16:44.530 --> 01:16:50.250
...as I Iive with you.

01:16:44.530 --> 01:16:50.250
anata to ikitaino

01:16:50.370 --> 01:16:56.380
Forever full up my Iove.

01:16:58.460 --> 01:17:08.470
I undo my hair and look up at Orion.

01:16:58.460 --> 01:17:08.470
kami wo hodoite miageru orion

01:17:09.260 --> 01:17:16.190
You feel so distant from me.

01:17:09.260 --> 01:17:16.190
anata ga tooku kanjiru

01:17:16.400 --> 01:17:18.730
As if to clean you away.

01:17:16.400 --> 01:17:18.730
uchikesu youni

01:17:18.730 --> 01:17:25.490
Your voice, your hair, even if...

01:17:18.730 --> 01:17:25.490
anata no koe anata no kami moshimo

01:17:26.740 --> 01:17:31.080
...we meet again after a thousand years,

01:17:26.740 --> 01:17:31.080
sennen tatte attemo

01:17:31.080 --> 01:17:36.710
I'll still be able to tell them apart.

01:17:31.080 --> 01:17:36.710
mada oboeteiru

01:17:37.290 --> 01:17:39.590
As many as there are stars above.

01:17:37.290 --> 01:17:39.590
hoshi no kazu hodo

01:17:39.590 --> 01:17:42.260
Memories of days passed,

01:17:39.590 --> 01:17:42.260
anohi no koto

01:17:42.260 --> 01:17:46.340
of the days to come, oh please...

01:17:42.260 --> 01:17:46.340
ashita no koto motto

01:17:47.090 --> 01:17:52.310
Give them to me, for I will never...

01:17:47.090 --> 01:17:52.310
omoide kudasai watashi wa

01:17:52.310 --> 01:17:58.190
...ever be able to purge myself of you.

01:17:52.310 --> 01:17:58.190
anata wo kesenakute

01:17:58.190 --> 01:18:04.610
Forever full up my love.
